This train journey has done its work.

00:30:11.323 --> 00:30:13.664
Chaplin never imagined he would achieve such fame.

00:30:15.096 --> 00:30:16.056
He now has a dream.

00:30:16.657 --> 00:30:17.577
to become a millionaire.

00:30:21.459 --> 00:30:25.400
For Chaplin, money was the lifeblood of the industry.

00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:26.661
He has always known how to be independent.

00:30:26.841 --> 00:30:27.701
That's truly its greatest strength.

00:30:27.741 --> 00:30:28.241
very early.

00:30:28.802 --> 00:30:29.422
Maturity,

00:30:29.722 --> 00:30:31.263
beyond the artist's genius,

00:30:31.403 --> 00:30:34.364
There is a businessman to target who realizes he needs to be independent.

00:30:35.504 --> 00:30:36.285
Having arrived in New York,

00:30:37.045 --> 00:30:39.086
Charlie and Sidney are waiting for their contact at the hotel.

00:30:40.246 --> 00:30:40.827
To relax,

00:30:40.867 --> 00:30:41.947
Charlie brought his violin.

00:30:42.807 --> 00:30:43.868
But after this long journey...

00:30:44.716 --> 00:30:45.516
If it lacks a little bit of...

00:30:45.564 --> 00:30:48.985
patience.

00:30:49.405 --> 00:30:51.266
Charlie played the violin very badly.

00:30:52.546 --> 00:30:53.486
really very bad,

00:30:54.407 --> 00:30:57.248
and his brother could no longer stand to hear him play the violin.

00:30:57.868 --> 00:30:58.368
SO,

00:30:58.588 --> 00:31:00.208
Since Charlie still wanted to play,

00:31:00.809 --> 00:31:04.910
He asked her to go to the bathroom and closed the door.

00:31:06.850 --> 00:31:08.991
When the representatives of the national force arrive,

00:31:09.791 --> 00:31:12.112
Charlie stays in the bathroom and lets his brother negotiate.

00:31:13.584 --> 00:31:16.386
He comes back after 15-20 minutes and says to Charlie,

00:31:17.307 --> 00:31:18.888
"They don't accept your proposal."

00:31:19.628 --> 00:31:21.970
They won't go beyond $500,000.

00:31:23.671 --> 00:31:25.973
Charlie continued playing the violin and said to him,

00:31:27.954 --> 00:31:28.394
" You know,

00:31:28.394 --> 00:31:28.894
Sidney,

00:31:29.455 --> 00:31:31.717
We were told we would get a million dollars.

00:31:32.858 --> 00:31:33.778
You should go back there.

00:31:36.240 --> 00:31:38.782
Sidney understands that the negotiation is only just beginning.

00:31:39.762 --> 00:31:41.884
He returns to see his brother several times.

00:31:42.452 --> 00:31:43.593
with new proposals,

00:31:44.333 --> 00:31:44.833
in vain.

00:31:52.498 --> 00:31:53.679
Sidney comes back and says

00:31:54.639 --> 00:31:56.660
Charlie, this is their final offer.

00:31:57.201 --> 00:31:58.301
They no longer want to negotiate.

00:31:58.902 --> 00:32:00.783
That's $750,000.

00:32:01.343 --> 00:32:02.024
Not one more.

00:32:04.605 --> 00:32:05.406
Charlie replies

00:32:07.046 --> 00:32:09.008
Tell them I'm an artist.

00:32:09.988 --> 00:32:11.609
I know nothing about money.

00:32:12.810 --> 00:32:14.092
But all I know,

00:32:14.512 --> 00:32:17.915
I want a million dollars.

00:32:20.037 --> 00:32:20.937
Ten minutes later,

00:32:21.378 --> 00:32:23.019
He comes back and writes,

00:32:23.519 --> 00:32:24.019
Charlie,

00:32:24.700 --> 00:32:25.561
Throw away your violin.

00:32:26.082 --> 00:32:27.503
You can buy yourself a cello,

00:32:28.223 --> 00:32:29.765
You have your million dollars.

00:32:32.287 --> 00:32:33.508
With his million dollars in his pocket,

00:32:34.569 --> 00:32:37.451
Chaplin is now free to do what he wants in Hollywood.

00:32:38.924 --> 00:32:41.045
He started by having his own studio built.

00:32:42.165 --> 00:32:46.447
A studio that reflects his personality, with offices and decor inspired by the London of his childhood.

00:32:49.468 --> 00:32:49.968
Obviously,

00:32:50.009 --> 00:32:50.969
He missed England.

00:32:52.009 --> 00:32:53.830
He had experienced many misfortunes there.

00:32:54.591 --> 00:32:55.671
But he liked being English.

00:32:57.572 --> 00:32:58.072
SO,

00:32:58.092 --> 00:33:01.733
This British-style studio reminded him of his roots.

00:33:03.054 --> 00:33:04.635
It was warmer for him.

00:33:05.375 --> 00:33:06.535
That's why he had it done that way.

00:33:08.216 --> 00:33:09.376
And in its new studios,

00:33:10.237 --> 00:33:11.437
Chaplin recreates a family.

00:33:12.397 --> 00:33:12.977
On camera,

00:33:13.858 --> 00:33:15.118
his faithful Rolly Tostrow,

00:33:15.938 --> 00:33:17.379
from whom he learned the art of filmmaking.

00:33:20.760 --> 00:33:22.020
Rolly was my grandfather.

00:33:23.860 --> 00:33:27.161
And he was Chaplin's cameraman for 38 years.

00:33:28.562 --> 00:33:30.122
Rolly was his closest confidant.

00:33:30.662 --> 00:33:31.162
He was helping him,

00:33:31.242 --> 00:33:32.203
Strictly speaking,

00:33:32.843 --> 00:33:33.663
to make his films.

00:33:34.483 --> 00:33:36.384
He really chooses who he's going to work with.

00:33:36.888 --> 00:33:38.309
And that's where a real period begins.

00:33:38.729 --> 00:33:39.229
It really is,

00:33:39.650 --> 00:33:41.131
He is at the height of his power.

00:33:41.892 --> 00:33:43.533
From now on, Chaplin is the sole master of the ship.

00:33:44.233 --> 00:33:45.074
He's acting,

00:33:45.754 --> 00:33:46.935
directs the other actors,

00:33:48.116 --> 00:33:50.257
He shoots and edits his own films.

00:33:51.879 --> 00:33:53.300
When he lacks inspiration,

00:33:53.940 --> 00:33:55.061
The entire machine stops.

00:33:56.082 --> 00:33:57.062
When an idea arises,

00:33:57.923 --> 00:33:59.424
everyone must be on high alert.

00:34:06.576 --> 00:34:09.317
He enjoyed tremendous freedom thanks to his success.

00:34:09.397 --> 00:34:12.538
thanks to his company and the money he earned.

00:34:13.378 --> 00:34:14.018
So for him,

00:34:14.019 --> 00:34:15.258
It wasn't about making money.

00:34:15.318 --> 00:34:17.119
It was about doing high-quality things.

00:34:18.159 --> 00:34:18.779
Whatever the cost.

00:34:20.460 --> 00:34:22.760
Charlie Chaplin's films enjoyed enormous popular success.

00:34:23.641 --> 00:34:24.141
Yet,

00:34:24.781 --> 00:34:26.741
The filmmaker is starting to have detractors.

00:34:28.202 --> 00:34:29.422
In the eyes of a certain segment of America,

00:34:30.142 --> 00:34:31.323
Chaplin remains an outsider.

00:34:31.743 --> 00:34:32.623
who made his fortune here

00:34:32.983 --> 00:34:35.464
but who refuses to take American citizenship.

00:34:36.268 --> 00:34:36.768
Worse,

00:34:36.868 --> 00:34:40.070
He uses his character to mock the system.

00:34:42.752 --> 00:34:46.934
A committee was formed in America to say that it was too violent.

00:34:47.995 --> 00:34:48.615
vulgar.

00:34:48.915 --> 00:34:51.677
He was showing off too much of his bourgeois side.

00:34:52.478 --> 00:34:55.059
A bit too anarchistic.

00:34:55.459 --> 00:34:57.080
and that he needed to calm down.

00:34:57.500 --> 00:34:59.782
He criticized people who had a lot of money.

00:34:59.783 --> 00:35:00.283
etc.

00:35:00.362 --> 00:35:03.384
and touched on aspects of society that no one had touched before.

00:35:09.848 --> 00:35:10.348
In humor,

00:35:10.448 --> 00:35:12.950
as soon as we gather together and as soon as it starts to make noise,

00:35:13.090 --> 00:35:15.372
Then things started to get a little tense.

00:35:15.772 --> 00:35:19.154
Characters like Chaplin are characters who have also been disturbing.

00:35:20.075 --> 00:35:20.735
In Washington,

00:35:21.736 --> 00:35:24.318
One man in particular already has Chaplin in his sights.

00:35:26.379 --> 00:35:28.361
His name is Jay Edgar Hoover.

00:35:29.121 --> 00:35:34.865
He is only 21 years old and has just been hired by the Department of Justice to monitor foreign nationals.

00:35:36.086 --> 00:35:39.088
A function that Chaplin recently ridiculed in his film The Immigrant.

00:35:40.204 --> 00:35:44.199
Hoover cannot stand it and he begins to take an interest in Chaplin's case.

00:35:46.576 --> 00:35:49.338
The fact that he did not want to take American citizenship,

00:35:49.898 --> 00:35:50.839
This creates suspicion.

00:35:50.859 --> 00:35:53.981
That is to say, he cannot be a good American since he is not even American.

00:35:54.141 --> 00:35:54.762
So right away,

00:35:54.763 --> 00:35:58.965
He becomes a target for Hoover because he is someone who is absolutely not a conformist.

00:35:59.265 --> 00:36:00.546
And the nonconformists,

00:36:00.646 --> 00:36:01.327
like Chaplin,

00:36:01.367 --> 00:36:02.788
This is the beginning of subversion for Hoover.

00:36:03.908 --> 00:36:07.051
Hoover is not yet the powerful head of the FBI.

00:36:09.112 --> 00:36:12.094
The Federal Bureau of Investigation would not be created until 7 years later.

00:36:13.095 --> 00:36:14.436
But he's already keeping an eye on Chaplin.

00:36:15.256 --> 00:36:18.037
And he soon discovers that he has a weakness.

00:36:31.060 --> 00:36:32.021
In 1918,

00:36:33.261 --> 00:36:36.562
The new fortunes of cinema are settling in the hills of Beverly Hills.

00:36:37.262 --> 00:36:38.962
where they organize decadent parties.

00:36:41.003 --> 00:36:43.084
It contains alcohol,

00:36:43.824 --> 00:36:44.384
drugs...

00:36:45.304 --> 00:36:46.184
and young actresses.

00:36:48.145 --> 00:36:52.746
Chaplin is of course a prominent member of what is known as the Hollywood colony.

00:36:57.367 --> 00:36:59.308
Many of his friends are lost in the party.

00:36:59.768 --> 00:37:02.129
He was very good at entertaining people.

00:37:03.889 --> 00:37:04.689
to amuse them,

00:37:04.709 --> 00:37:05.510
to make them laugh.

00:37:05.870 --> 00:37:06.470
He had all that.

00:37:06.550 --> 00:37:07.790
But I think he never did that.

00:37:08.250 --> 00:37:09.531
He never got lost in that.

00:37:10.471 --> 00:37:10.971
For him,

00:37:11.831 --> 00:37:12.371
no alcohol,

00:37:12.451 --> 00:37:12.951
no drugs.

00:37:13.912 --> 00:37:14.472
On the other hand...

00:37:15.392 --> 00:37:16.072
He likes women,

00:37:16.873 --> 00:37:17.393
and above all

00:37:18.133 --> 00:37:18.914
very young women.

00:37:22.355 --> 00:37:23.155
At one of his parties,

00:37:23.156 --> 00:37:24.656
He meets Mildred Harris.

00:37:25.176 --> 00:37:26.237
It was at Sam Goldwyn's house.

00:37:26.357 --> 00:37:28.258
at whose house he used to play poker.

00:37:29.018 --> 00:37:29.958
She was as short as he was.

00:37:30.479 --> 00:37:32.059
and he liked girls his own height,

00:37:32.119 --> 00:37:33.100
if you know what I mean.

00:37:35.501 --> 00:37:38.062
Mildred Harris dreams of becoming an actress.

00:37:38.842 --> 00:37:39.923
She was only 16 years old at the time.

00:37:42.083 --> 00:37:43.164
Chaplin falls under her spell.

00:37:44.236 --> 00:37:45.257
But the idyll will be brief.

00:37:50.559 --> 00:37:52.160
He thought Mildred Harris was very pretty.

00:37:52.701 --> 00:37:55.502
But Chaplin himself said that she wasn't very intelligent.

00:37:55.742 --> 00:37:57.523
He thought they were incompatible.

00:37:58.944 --> 00:38:00.645
But Mildred is more cunning than she appears.

00:38:01.846 --> 00:38:04.167
She has no intention of letting Hollywood's best catch slip away.

00:38:05.207 --> 00:38:06.608
A few weeks after they met,

00:38:07.148 --> 00:38:08.609
She tells him that she is pregnant.

00:38:09.510 --> 00:38:10.430
Chaplin gets scared.

00:38:11.051 --> 00:38:11.891
Mildred is a minor.

00:38:12.671 --> 00:38:13.532
He risks going to prison.

00:38:14.592 --> 00:38:15.613
He is forced to marry her.

00:38:19.315 --> 00:38:19.996
Mildred Harris,

00:38:20.076 --> 00:38:21.817
like many young girls in Hollywood,

00:38:21.997 --> 00:38:23.058
he was thinking about his career.

00:38:24.159 --> 00:38:26.700
And becoming Mrs. Chaplin could certainly have helped her.

00:38:27.581 --> 00:38:29.342
So she made him believe she was pregnant.

00:38:29.582 --> 00:38:30.783
But in reality, she wasn't.

00:38:31.724 --> 00:38:34.506
They got married and she became pregnant after the wedding.

00:38:36.547 --> 00:38:37.968
Chaplin fell into the trap.

00:38:39.069 --> 00:38:40.390
Married to a woman he doesn't love,

00:38:41.451 --> 00:38:43.472
He enters a period of artistic stagnation.

00:38:48.541 --> 00:38:54.165
It is certain that his marriage to Mildred Harris was a kind of creative block.

00:38:55.406 --> 00:38:56.387
He was starting to make films.

00:38:56.727 --> 00:38:57.528
He abandoned them.

00:39:03.532 --> 00:39:06.294
To escape this forced marriage and rediscover his love of cinema,

00:39:06.995 --> 00:39:08.356
in January 1919,

00:39:09.096 --> 00:39:10.777
Chaplin launches United Artists,

00:39:11.558 --> 00:39:14.460
a new film company founded with his two best friends.

00:39:15.288 --> 00:39:18.629
The acting couple Douglas Fairbank and Mary Pickford.

00:39:19.829 --> 00:39:22.830
It was Douglas and Mary who convinced him to come and live near them.

00:39:24.290 --> 00:39:24.790
Charlie,

00:39:24.991 --> 00:39:27.351
Douglas and Mary were like brother and sister.

00:39:28.032 --> 00:39:28.812
They loved each other that much.

00:39:29.872 --> 00:39:30.932
On the day of the signing,

00:39:31.873 --> 00:39:32.533
as per usual,

00:39:33.333 --> 00:39:36.014
Chaplin makes people laugh and saves appearances.

00:39:37.674 --> 00:39:40.495
But the drama he is experiencing at home is only getting worse.

00:39:41.575 --> 00:39:42.075
Norman,

00:39:42.896 --> 00:39:44.096
the child Mildred is carrying,

00:39:44.972 --> 00:39:46.093
has a malformation.

00:39:47.554 --> 00:39:49.214
He died three days after his birth.

00:39:51.216 --> 00:39:51.716
Obviously,

00:39:51.956 --> 00:39:53.857
It was a tough blow for Chaplin.

00:39:54.658 --> 00:39:55.638
But it's strange because,

00:39:56.239 --> 00:39:57.339
From that moment on,

00:39:57.959 --> 00:40:00.161
He had the idea of ​​making a film with a child.

00:40:02.002 --> 00:40:02.602
At 30 years old,

00:40:03.603 --> 00:40:06.604
devastated by the loss of his first child and the failure of his marriage,

00:40:07.365 --> 00:40:12.748
Chaplin then went back to work to extract one of his greatest masterpieces from his personal tragedy.

00:40:15.949 --> 00:40:17.650
Four days after the death of his son,

00:40:17.990 --> 00:40:20.012
Chaplin auditioned young boys at the studio.

00:40:21.713 --> 00:40:22.333
Initially,

00:40:23.034 --> 00:40:25.195
He was looking for children for one of his productions.

00:40:25.956 --> 00:40:26.656
"Charlot Picnic".

00:40:27.437 --> 00:40:28.278
But during the casting process,

00:40:29.058 --> 00:40:31.720
A boy will move him so much that he hires him on the spot.

00:40:32.681 --> 00:40:33.802
His name is Jackie Coogan.

00:40:34.562 --> 00:40:36.123
He was saying something about Jackie Coogan.

00:40:36.644 --> 00:40:37.364
I don't know why,

00:40:37.404 --> 00:40:38.665
But every time I see that boy,

00:40:38.725 --> 00:40:39.446
I feel like crying.

00:40:41.707 --> 00:40:42.628
A few days later...

00:40:43.480 --> 00:40:46.981
Bankers and foreign investors are visiting the studios.

00:40:47.862 --> 00:40:49.702
It has been months since Chaplin produced a film.

00:40:50.502 --> 00:40:51.443
The atmosphere is heavy,

00:40:52.083 --> 00:40:55.784
But Jackie Coogan's company will help to reassure the financiers.

00:40:59.745 --> 00:41:00.786
They put on his Chaplin uniform.

00:41:00.826 --> 00:41:01.506
They are very happy.

00:41:01.606 --> 00:41:02.286
They play with the kid.

00:41:02.366 --> 00:41:02.907
Jackie Coogan,

00:41:03.367 --> 00:41:05.507
of which they have absolutely no idea what he will do with it.

00:41:06.088 --> 00:41:07.048
and to amuse the bankers.

00:41:13.201 --> 00:41:13.801
He said,

00:41:14.102 --> 00:41:17.224
Jackie is so malleable that when I show her something,

00:41:17.665 --> 00:41:19.927
He manages to do it exactly as I show him.

00:41:20.527 --> 00:41:23.910
He does it again and again without losing spontaneity or emotion.

00:41:25.111 --> 00:41:28.494
He truly felt that he had found the perfect actor in Jackie Coogan.

00:41:30.096 --> 00:41:31.837
Jackie reassured investors,

00:41:32.317 --> 00:41:33.679
but above all he inspired Chaplin.

00:41:34.880 --> 00:41:37.082
He then had the idea for his first feature film,

00:41:37.902 --> 00:41:39.644
in which Charlie Chaplin would adopt a child.

00:41:40.696 --> 00:41:43.158
He will simply call him the Kid.

00:41:44.739 --> 00:41:45.239
Therefore,

00:41:45.920 --> 00:41:47.081
A wound is reopening.

00:41:47.861 --> 00:41:49.482
A figure from the past reappears.

00:41:50.343 --> 00:41:51.163
His mother's,

00:41:51.624 --> 00:41:52.124
Anna.

00:41:52.925 --> 00:41:56.087
And this tragedy of abandonment that they experienced side by side,

00:41:57.087 --> 00:41:57.587
Mother and son.

00:42:08.587 --> 00:42:09.168
At the end of the

00:42:09.608 --> 00:42:10.108
19th century,

00:42:11.129 --> 00:42:13.511
Anna Chaplin is a musical artist.

00:42:15.133 --> 00:42:16.494
She is raising her two sons alone.

00:42:17.255 --> 00:42:18.796
Charlie and Sidney.

00:42:20.197 --> 00:42:22.419
Since his divorce from Charles Chaplin Senior,

00:42:23.580 --> 00:42:26.122
All she has to offer her sons is the misery of Kennington Road.

00:42:31.427 --> 00:42:32.728
Even when she was at rock bottom,

00:42:32.808 --> 00:42:35.230
She taught them a love of theatre and creativity.

00:42:37.747 --> 00:42:39.288
She told them biblical stories,

00:42:39.728 --> 00:42:42.089
entertained them with anecdotes from musicals,

00:42:43.009 --> 00:42:45.450
And he said she was a wonderful imitator.

00:42:46.931 --> 00:42:47.611
But Anna is unwell.

00:42:48.592 --> 00:42:49.972
She hasn't worked for a long time.

00:42:50.613 --> 00:42:53.574
She spends entire days at home calling out to people in the street.

00:42:54.954 --> 00:42:55.454
Actually,

00:42:56.075 --> 00:42:58.336
She is slowly descending into madness.

00:42:59.736 --> 00:43:02.418
He watched her gradually become depressed and psychotic.

00:43:02.878 --> 00:43:05.619
She was looking out the window; what she was saying made no sense.

00:43:06.551 --> 00:43:07.571
He witnessed all of that.

00:43:07.711 --> 00:43:08.732
It broke his heart.

00:43:08.752 --> 00:43:11.253
In 1898,

00:43:13.553 --> 00:43:15.354
Anna is interned at the Canhille asylum.

00:43:16.754 --> 00:43:18.015
Doctors are alarmed.

00:43:19.015 --> 00:43:19.896
The case is very serious.

00:43:24.337 --> 00:43:27.058
His mental illness was a consequence of a venereal disease.

00:43:27.878 --> 00:43:29.139
more specifically syphilis.

00:43:35.603 --> 00:43:37.544
She was believed to have suffered from stage 3 syphilis.

00:43:38.465 --> 00:43:41.746
The doctors said that this was the cause of his madness because at level 3,

00:43:41.866 --> 00:43:43.207
It is the nervous system that is affected.

00:43:45.187 --> 00:43:47.768
Charlie will never know how his mother contracted this disease.

00:43:49.229 --> 00:43:51.070
Anna was a fickle woman who loved men.

00:43:53.351 --> 00:43:56.952
He spent several months at the orphanage until he returned home.

00:43:59.873 --> 00:44:01.074
But a few years later,

00:44:02.374 --> 00:44:03.555
She's having a terrible relapse.

00:44:07.516 --> 00:44:08.016
A day,

00:44:08.316 --> 00:44:09.497
Children came to tell him,

00:44:09.997 --> 00:44:11.017
Your mother has gone crazy.

00:44:11.738 --> 00:44:14.639
She is in the street and she is distributing pieces of coal to passers-by.

00:44:16.320 --> 00:44:18.381
He had to go and get her to take her to the hospice.

00:44:18.681 --> 00:44:19.321
then to the asylum.

00:44:22.082 --> 00:44:22.642
And this time,

00:44:23.943 --> 00:44:26.064
Charlie will have to take her back to the asylum himself.

00:44:27.304 --> 00:44:28.525
He is now 14 years old.

00:44:29.345 --> 00:44:30.166
lives alone with her.

00:44:31.166 --> 00:44:32.867
His brother Sidney joined the navy.

00:44:40.277 --> 00:44:44.620
The image of a 14-year-old boy having to take his poor, mentally ill mother to the hospital,

00:44:46.261 --> 00:44:47.042
leave her there,

00:44:47.722 --> 00:44:49.504
then leave alone.

00:44:49.704 --> 00:44:53.466
It's a terrible image we have of Chaplin's life at that time.

00:44:55.928 --> 00:44:56.929
From this day forward,

00:44:59.071 --> 00:45:01.372
Anna will never leave the psychiatric hospital again.

00:45:05.415 --> 00:45:06.815
Charlie finds himself completely alone.

00:45:08.096 --> 00:45:10.036
but he refuses to return to the orphanage.

00:45:11.897 --> 00:45:14.518
The London orphanage of that time,

00:45:14.638 --> 00:45:15.358
It was very, very hard.

00:45:15.418 --> 00:45:16.958
It was like being in prison.

00:45:17.919 --> 00:45:20.239
So all of this deeply traumatized him.

00:45:21.560 --> 00:45:22.580
And he was very proud,

00:45:22.900 --> 00:45:23.660
He was left alone.

00:45:24.100 --> 00:45:25.321
People offered him help,

00:45:25.581 --> 00:45:26.101
He said no.

00:45:26.221 --> 00:45:26.721
How's it going.

00:45:27.501 --> 00:45:28.342
For several months,

00:45:29.202 --> 00:45:30.762
Charlie survives by working here and there.

00:45:31.762 --> 00:45:32.064
Sometimes,

00:45:32.064 --> 00:45:33.383
He is forced to sleep in the street.

00:45:34.839 --> 00:45:37.202
The situation continued until his brother Sidney,

00:45:37.242 --> 00:45:38.464
back in England,

00:45:38.864 --> 00:45:39.825
eventually find him.

00:45:41.307 --> 00:45:43.089
When Sidney returned from South Africa,

00:45:43.109 --> 00:45:44.371
He took Charlie under his wing.

00:45:44.731 --> 00:45:49.658
He helped him financially until he found him a job in the theatre.

00:45:50.799 --> 00:45:51.660
Effective from this day forward,

00:45:52.721 --> 00:45:53.883
The two brothers will never leave each other's side again.

00:46:02.939 --> 00:46:04.600
All the memories of that difficult childhood,

00:46:05.580 --> 00:46:06.561
his feeling of abandonment,

00:46:07.721 --> 00:46:09.282
Chaplin instilled them in the kid.

00:46:10.662 --> 00:46:12.143
He manages to transcend his grief.

00:46:12.483 --> 00:46:13.823
But a new challenge awaits him.

00:46:16.365 --> 00:46:17.705
As filming draws to a close,

00:46:18.605 --> 00:46:20.606
His wife Mildred launches an attack.

00:46:21.327 --> 00:46:24.248
She accuses him in the press of having deserted the marital home.

00:46:25.548 --> 00:46:26.169
I didn't see Mr.

00:46:26.309 --> 00:46:27.489
Chaplin for the past two weeks,

00:46:27.949 --> 00:46:29.470
And I haven't lived with him for months.

00:46:30.130 --> 00:46:31.071
I conclude that he has left me.

00:46:32.215 --> 00:46:32.935
During this time,

00:46:33.876 --> 00:46:38.218
His lawyers are launching divorce proceedings and planning to ruin the filmmaker.

00:46:38.899 --> 00:46:41.520
Mrs. Chaplin asks the court to freeze the funds committed by Mr.

00:46:41.700 --> 00:46:43.181
Chaplin in several films.

00:46:43.801 --> 00:46:46.203
Funds estimated at over $500,000.

00:46:46.603 --> 00:46:47.103
In other words,

00:46:47.824 --> 00:46:49.525
The lawyers are demanding the kid's tapes.

00:46:50.325 --> 00:46:52.806
But Chaplin has no intention of letting his film be stolen.

00:46:53.527 --> 00:46:54.107
In the middle of the night,

00:46:54.748 --> 00:46:55.808
He wakes up his entire team.

00:46:56.929 --> 00:46:58.590
Grandfather says that he came to his house,

00:46:59.010 --> 00:47:00.611
knocked on the door and said...

00:47:01.319 --> 00:47:01.901
Come to the studio,

00:47:02.181 --> 00:47:02.843
includes the films,

00:47:02.923 --> 00:47:03.584
We have to leave.

00:47:11.619 --> 00:47:14.341
He had to take the film negatives to Salt Lake City.

00:47:14.461 --> 00:47:15.562
then in New Jersey.

00:47:18.024 --> 00:47:22.186
He wanted to escape the bailiffs who were seeking to reclaim them as joint property.

00:47:23.487 --> 00:47:27.152
They could have taken everything from him and he was very afraid of that.

00:47:30.497 --> 00:47:31.258
For weeks,

00:47:32.159 --> 00:47:37.507
He travels across the United States from hotel to hotel, always one step ahead of the bailiffs.

00:47:43.084 --> 00:47:46.106
It was a kind of Chaplin film that was unfolding in parallel.

00:47:46.146 --> 00:47:49.549
He walked through hotel lobbies dressed as a woman so that no one would recognize him.

00:47:50.669 --> 00:47:53.331
He was going to hide in the desert with his reels of film.

00:48:03.619 --> 00:48:04.920
He's the character from those movies,

00:48:05.160 --> 00:48:08.462
That is to say, the whole world is turning against him.

00:48:09.707 --> 00:48:10.988
Well, despite its small size,

00:48:11.588 --> 00:48:12.608
He's getting a real beating.

00:48:12.828 --> 00:48:14.369
But the guy just keeps going.

00:48:19.472 --> 00:48:19.972
Eventually,

00:48:20.832 --> 00:48:24.354
This whole story comes to an end after a long legal and media battle.

00:48:27.955 --> 00:48:30.156
The divorce was finalized in November 1920.

00:48:31.497 --> 00:48:35.459
Mildred Harris receives $200,000 and half of Chaplin's estate.

00:48:36.759 --> 00:48:37.560
In return,

00:48:38.340 --> 00:48:39.341
He was able to save his film.

00:48:41.763 --> 00:48:43.505
The kit was released in theaters two months later.

00:48:44.926 --> 00:48:47.508
His success surpassed anything Chaplin had experienced before.

00:48:49.549 --> 00:48:53.292
The reviews are said to be scathing and crowds are flocking to all the cinemas.

00:48:54.133 --> 00:48:55.774
The film has been sold in 50 countries.

00:48:56.995 --> 00:48:57.916
This is a new record.

00:49:09.432 --> 00:49:13.034
That's his greatest achievement.

00:49:14.275 --> 00:49:19.759
The way he manages to make you laugh and cry at the same time.

00:49:25.683 --> 00:49:26.243
For the first time,

00:49:26.244 --> 00:49:28.024
There are some very, very dramatic scenes in The Kid.

00:49:28.025 --> 00:49:30.006
In particular, at one point Daz goes to get the child.

00:49:35.095 --> 00:49:36.676
We see Jackie Coogan stretching his arms out like this.

00:49:36.677 --> 00:49:37.496
We see Chaplin taking them,

00:49:37.756 --> 00:49:39.717
The violins are screaming from all sides,

00:49:40.377 --> 00:49:41.897
He continues across the rooftops.

00:49:41.898 --> 00:49:42.398
the car,

00:49:42.737 --> 00:49:44.098
He even goes so far as to get into a fight with someone.

00:49:44.258 --> 00:49:46.039
very strong elements that did not exist before in Chaplin's work,

00:49:46.339 --> 00:49:47.619
He enters a truly dramatic world.

00:50:00.079 --> 00:50:04.162
It was the first film in which he had really drawn on his childhood memories.

00:50:08.486 --> 00:50:09.567
But the most moving thing,

00:50:09.987 --> 00:50:11.428
It was because he had just lost his child.

00:50:27.541 --> 00:50:27.882
A few

00:50:27.882 --> 00:50:29.123
weeks after the release of The Kid,

00:50:30.039 --> 00:50:32.041
Chaplin experiences another upheaval in his life.

00:50:33.262 --> 00:50:33.762
His mother,

00:50:34.083 --> 00:50:34.583
Anna,

00:50:35.104 --> 00:50:35.985
arrives in the United States.

00:50:37.066 --> 00:50:38.527
After more than ten years of separation,

00:50:38.547 --> 00:50:40.189
He decided to bring her to Hollywood.

00:50:40.949 --> 00:50:43.392
One of her assistants went to pick her up at the port of New York,

00:50:44.233 --> 00:50:45.854
But the reunion looks set to be complicated.

00:50:49.676 --> 00:50:52.997
She seemed really well and she went to the immigration office.

00:50:54.298 --> 00:50:56.860
When the agent asked her, "Are you Charles Chaplin's mother?"

00:50:57.460 --> 00:50:58.100
She replied, "Yes,

00:50:58.741 --> 00:50:59.741
And you,
you are Jesus Christ.”

00:51:01.222 --> 00:51:02.322
It could have gone badly,

00:51:02.743 --> 00:51:03.243
But no,

00:51:03.623 --> 00:51:05.124
and she was able to go live in California.

00:51:07.926 --> 00:51:10.787
Charlie found him a small house north of Hollywood.

00:51:11.948 --> 00:51:13.689
She would spend the last eight years of her life there.

00:51:15.550 --> 00:51:17.150
Anna receives many visitors.

00:51:18.171 --> 00:51:19.112
but rarely his son.

00:51:27.700 --> 00:51:29.521
There was a couple who took care of her.

00:51:30.482 --> 00:51:31.363
All she wanted,

00:51:31.563 --> 00:51:32.063
She had it.

00:51:33.285 --> 00:51:35.347
But it was very depressing for him to go see her.

00:51:38.369 --> 00:51:40.371
What stands out most to me,

00:51:40.451 --> 00:51:40.951
I believe,

00:51:41.753 --> 00:51:44.355
It was about being confronted with his mother's madness.

00:51:48.260 --> 00:51:49.380
The mother he had loved,

00:51:50.140 --> 00:51:51.281
the mother of his memories,

00:51:51.341 --> 00:51:51.921
was beautiful

00:51:52.181 --> 00:51:52.961
talented,

00:51:53.441 --> 00:51:54.362
full of vitality.

00:51:56.942 --> 00:51:58.983
The woman she had become was psychotic.

00:51:59.563 --> 00:52:00.063
obese,

00:52:00.343 --> 00:52:01.244
old before her time,

00:52:01.704 --> 00:52:04.244
a character who is both sad and tragic.

00:52:05.585 --> 00:52:13.207
His grandmother and mother ended up in psychiatric institutions.

00:52:14.095 --> 00:52:17.898
And I think he also had a slight fear of one day going crazy.

00:52:19.760 --> 00:52:20.961
This is Chaplin's great tragedy,

00:52:22.082 --> 00:52:24.604
the one he will try to exorcise in his love life.

00:52:26.106 --> 00:52:28.007
This happy memory of a young and beautiful mother,

00:52:28.868 --> 00:52:31.510
He will relentlessly search for him in his romantic conquests.

00:52:32.451 --> 00:52:35.534
This explains a little why he was attracted to young girls.

00:52:36.174 --> 00:52:38.096
Not out of an obsession with young girls,

00:52:38.797 --> 00:52:41.119
but above all out of fear of old age.

00:52:42.507 --> 00:52:44.890
And three years after his divorce from Mildred Harris,

00:52:46.052 --> 00:52:47.073
Chaplin falls in love again.

00:52:48.555 --> 00:52:49.516
In love once again,

00:52:50.538 --> 00:52:51.339
of a teenage girl.

00:52:55.881 --> 00:52:56.462
With Lockheed,

00:52:57.523 --> 00:52:58.884
Chaplin developed a taste for feature films.

00:53:01.287 --> 00:53:02.288
In 1924,

00:53:02.308 --> 00:53:04.310
He is embarking on a monumental project.

00:53:04.750 --> 00:53:05.531
The Street and Verlore.

00:53:07.013 --> 00:53:07.994
Natural settings,

00:53:08.535 --> 00:53:11.237
over 600 extras and a budget of $2 million,

00:53:12.118 --> 00:53:13.420
It's the most expensive film of the year.

00:53:18.542 --> 00:53:25.729
They had hired a group of bums in Sacramento and brought them in by train to film the opening scene.

00:53:28.451 --> 00:53:29.572
It was quite difficult,

00:53:29.953 --> 00:53:31.314
in the middle of all this snow,

00:53:31.594 --> 00:53:34.417
trying to control the holds and everything that was happening.

00:53:38.760 --> 00:53:40.882
Charlie Chaplin also takes on a new dimension in this film.

00:53:41.863 --> 00:53:43.164
A more philosophical dimension.

00:53:44.125 --> 00:53:45.446
Chaplin returns to his major themes.

00:53:46.187 --> 00:53:46.687
love,

00:53:46.867 --> 00:53:47.367
hunger,

00:53:47.468 --> 00:53:49.270
poverty and lack of gain.

00:53:50.431 --> 00:53:52.332
Some scenes will become iconic.

00:54:23.253 --> 00:54:27.584
But the filming will once again be disrupted by Chaplin's private life.

00:54:28.948 --> 00:54:30.111
That young actress behind him...

00:54:31.053 --> 00:54:32.234
Her name is Lita Gray.

00:54:33.195 --> 00:54:33.855
She is 15 years old.

00:54:34.716 --> 00:54:35.656
At the start of filming,

00:54:35.696 --> 00:54:36.917
She plays the lead role.

00:54:37.858 --> 00:54:39.839
Chaplin had met her during the casting of The Kid,

00:54:40.720 --> 00:54:41.400
three years earlier.

00:54:42.941 --> 00:54:45.063
Charlie was looking for a pretty girl for the Kid.

00:54:48.465 --> 00:54:49.366
She introduced herself,

00:54:50.006 --> 00:54:51.567
She was wearing her mother's heels.

00:54:52.048 --> 00:54:54.689
She had put her hair up and she went through the audition.

00:54:56.010 --> 00:54:57.211
Chaplin liked her very much.

00:54:58.952 --> 00:54:59.493
According to Lita,

00:54:59.997 --> 00:55:05.464
He supposedly created that dream sequence in The Kid solely to offer him the character of the angel.

00:55:06.525 --> 00:55:08.708
In this surreal and premonitory sequence,

00:55:09.409 --> 00:55:11.251
Charlie Chaplin had to resist the angel of temptation.

00:55:12.012 --> 00:55:13.434
portrayed by the young Lita Gray,

00:55:14.255 --> 00:55:15.316
then only aged

00:55:15.716 --> 00:55:16.216
12 years old.

00:55:28.394 --> 00:55:33.418
None of Chaplin's associates thought she was particularly photogenic or talented.

00:55:34.339 --> 00:55:35.379
But she was engaged.

00:55:36.080 --> 00:55:39.623
because Chaplin was enthusiastic and no one opposed his enthusiasm.

00:55:41.064 --> 00:55:41.925
Three years later,

00:55:42.665 --> 00:55:44.847
Chaplin therefore hired him again for the gold rush.

00:55:45.868 --> 00:55:47.690
But they have an affair during filming.

00:55:48.430 --> 00:55:49.791
and the girl becomes pregnant.

00:55:50.672 --> 00:55:52.093
She then has to give up her role.

00:55:54.275 --> 00:55:56.017
Chaplin suggested that she have an abortion.

00:55:56.905 --> 00:55:58.546
But Lita's family said no.

00:55:59.187 --> 00:56:01.909
and they insisted that they get married.

00:56:03.590 --> 00:56:08.274
The marriage was celebrated in Mexico and made official in the press on November 26, 1924.

00:56:09.115 --> 00:56:09.896
For the second time,

00:56:10.596 --> 00:56:13.579
Chaplin has just married a teenage girl to avoid prison.

00:56:17.342 --> 00:56:18.382
He told her immediately,

00:56:18.703 --> 00:56:20.684
I have no intention of being a husband to you.

00:56:21.825 --> 00:56:23.487
I will be there for social reasons.

00:56:24.507 --> 00:56:26.149
But there will be nothing else.

00:56:28.041 --> 00:56:30.222
Charlie will, however, have two children with Lita.

00:56:31.283 --> 00:56:31.943
Charles Junior,

00:56:32.764 --> 00:56:33.284
then Sidney.

00:56:34.485 --> 00:56:35.385
But that doesn't change anything.

00:56:36.125 --> 00:56:37.666
The young woman feels neglected.

00:56:38.427 --> 00:56:39.267
then at 18 years old,

00:56:39.307 --> 00:56:42.409
She leaves the marital home and files for divorce.

00:56:46.791 --> 00:56:48.993
It was worse than her first divorce.

00:56:49.473 --> 00:56:52.014
They fought it out in the press with sensational headlines.

00:56:52.755 --> 00:56:53.395
In the press,

00:56:54.015 --> 00:56:57.017
Lita Gray paints a scathing portrait of the father of her children.

00:56:57.865 --> 00:57:00.027
Further tarnishing Chaplin's image.

00:57:00.967 --> 00:57:06.892
Mrs. Chaplin states that the actor threatened her twice with a revolver and suggested she commit suicide.

00:57:07.932 --> 00:57:11.995
It is said that her hair turned white around the time of her divorce from Lita Gray.

00:57:12.576 --> 00:57:13.817
almost overnight.

00:57:23.785 --> 00:57:25.946
It's still amazing to see that Charlie Chaplin,

00:57:26.006 --> 00:57:27.907
who observed human nature so well,

00:57:28.787 --> 00:57:33.289
was unable to see his own flaws.

00:57:46.675 --> 00:57:47.856
Meanwhile in Washington,

00:57:48.917 --> 00:57:49.597
his worst enemy,

00:57:50.478 --> 00:57:50.818
J.

00:57:50.818 --> 00:57:51.619
Edgar Hoover,

00:57:52.199 --> 00:57:55.021
has just taken up his duties as head of the FBI.

00:57:55.902 --> 00:57:56.762
His first target,

00:57:57.483 --> 00:57:57.983
Hollywood.

00:57:58.924 --> 00:58:01.145
Accused by the leagues of corrupting America,

00:58:01.946 --> 00:58:04.267
He is determined to restore order and morality there.

00:58:04.287 --> 00:58:06.229
What bothers him about Hollywood,

00:58:07.029 --> 00:58:08.410
It's amplified tenfold by Chaplin.

00:58:08.470 --> 00:58:11.853
That is to say, there is a space for freedom in Hollywood,

00:58:13.054 --> 00:58:14.875
whether at the political level or at the level of morals.

00:58:15.379 --> 00:58:17.019
that it doesn't exist anywhere else in American society.

00:58:17.420 --> 00:58:20.961
What Hoover deeply disliked about Chaplin,

00:58:21.221 --> 00:58:21.861
That's his freedom.

00:58:22.741 --> 00:58:25.862
But the filmmaker does not yet sense this growing threat.

00:58:26.582 --> 00:58:27.322
because for the moment,

00:58:28.083 --> 00:58:29.403
He has other concerns.

00:58:35.465 --> 00:58:36.485
In the late 1920s,

00:58:36.985 --> 00:58:38.085
Everything is falling apart in Hollywood.

00:58:38.545 --> 00:58:44.267
The 1929 financial crisis shook the American economy and did not spare the film industry.

00:58:44.827 --> 00:58:46.748
Studios are closing one after another.

00:58:46.968 --> 00:58:48.589
Chaplin received better advice.

00:58:49.070 --> 00:58:51.151
He had time to secure his fortune.

00:58:51.591 --> 00:58:53.252
But there is something else that worries him.

00:58:53.652 --> 00:58:55.313
The arrival of a technological revolution,

00:58:55.673 --> 00:58:56.674
talking pictures.

00:58:57.314 --> 00:58:58.095
Buster Keaton,

00:58:58.255 --> 00:58:58.915
L'Oréal and Hardy,

00:58:59.035 --> 00:59:00.676
all the stars of his generation,

00:59:01.217 --> 00:59:01.957
have fallen into oblivion.

00:59:02.577 --> 00:59:05.679
So what will Charlie Chaplin do in the face of this major upheaval?

00:59:06.059 --> 00:59:07.440
He, who has always been at the forefront,

00:59:07.441 --> 00:59:08.581
at the forefront of modernity,

00:59:09.201 --> 00:59:11.583
persists in believing in the future of mature cinema.

00:59:17.087 --> 00:59:18.148
In the late 1920s,

00:59:18.968 --> 00:59:20.810
Concern is growing at the Chaplin studio.

00:59:22.111 --> 00:59:23.351
The return of theaters is not good.

00:59:24.272 --> 00:59:26.674
All the recent silent films have not been successful.

00:59:29.576 --> 00:59:30.456
During depression,

00:59:31.077 --> 00:59:32.138
Things were tough,

00:59:33.038 --> 00:59:34.519
Many studios had closed.

00:59:36.421 --> 00:59:38.342
Chaplin had just divorced Lita Gray,

00:59:39.443 --> 00:59:40.904
So he had a lot of money problems.

00:59:43.486 --> 00:59:45.467
Chaplin felt the pressure mounting from all sides.

00:59:46.419 --> 00:59:48.740
This, incidentally, inspired a scene in his new film.

00:59:49.140 --> 00:59:49.660
the circus.

01:00:04.467 --> 01:00:05.327
For the first time,

01:00:05.948 --> 01:00:07.368
Chaplin no longer fills theaters.

01:00:09.269 --> 01:00:11.010
The circus was his first commercial failure.

01:00:12.050 --> 01:00:13.531
Charlie is worried about what will happen next.

01:00:14.600 --> 01:00:15.440
A talking film

01:00:15.820 --> 01:00:16.541
a silent film,

01:00:16.661 --> 01:00:17.361
What does my future hold?

01:00:18.122 --> 01:00:19.563
Nobody knew what was going to happen.

01:00:20.163 --> 01:00:21.604
It was the beginning of the end for everyone.

01:00:22.825 --> 01:00:23.666
They were devastated.

01:00:24.306 --> 01:00:24.787
From now on,

01:00:24.787 --> 01:00:25.787
Everything had changed for them.

01:00:27.188 --> 01:00:28.389
Even his own brother,

01:00:28.509 --> 01:00:29.009
Sidney,

01:00:29.710 --> 01:00:30.971
usually so optimistic,

01:00:31.591 --> 01:00:32.392
feels the wind changing.

01:00:34.033 --> 01:00:36.195
They have just narrowly escaped the stock market crash.

01:00:36.955 --> 01:00:39.077
With everything they've earned in the last 15 years,

01:00:39.837 --> 01:00:42.379
They can live very comfortably until the end of their days.

01:00:43.407 --> 01:00:45.989
Sidney then suggests they set sail.

01:00:48.671 --> 01:00:49.432
He told Charlie,

01:00:50.053 --> 01:00:50.433
It's good,

01:00:50.433 --> 01:00:51.154
We've done enough.

01:00:51.174 --> 01:00:51.674
We stop.

01:00:52.174 --> 01:00:52.815
And Charlie said,

01:00:53.495 --> 01:00:53.995
not me.

01:00:54.857 --> 01:00:55.557
When his brother told him,

01:00:55.558 --> 01:00:56.178
The visiting room is arriving.

01:00:56.179 --> 01:00:56.679
We stop everything.

01:00:56.679 --> 01:00:57.078
We have enough.

01:00:57.078 --> 01:00:57.539
etc.

01:00:57.539 --> 01:00:58.040
He said,
no,

01:00:58.040 --> 01:00:58.920
I still have things to say.

01:00:58.921 --> 01:01:00.461
I'll say it like that because that's how I know how to do it.

01:01:01.002 --> 01:01:01.662
And Sidney said,

01:01:01.862 --> 01:01:02.363
I'm stopping.

01:01:02.603 --> 01:01:03.103
And he did it.

01:01:04.945 --> 01:01:06.927
Sidney returns to Europe to live out his days happily.

01:01:08.688 --> 01:01:12.191
Charlie thus finds himself alone to face the end of the silent era.

01:01:16.188 --> 01:01:18.189
He made so many beautiful silent films,

01:01:18.729 --> 01:01:20.090
all great successes.

01:01:20.731 --> 01:01:25.915
And then comes a technological revolution that he doesn't quite know how to handle.

01:01:26.355 --> 01:01:30.138
So he was cautious about talking films.

01:01:31.759 --> 01:01:34.461
Chaplin had another problem with the arrival of talking pictures.

01:01:35.361 --> 01:01:36.422
He hates his own voice.

01:01:38.904 --> 01:01:41.606
Can he continue to be Charlie Chaplin and speak at the same time?

01:01:41.686 --> 01:01:42.947
Because Charlie doesn't speak.

01:01:43.871 --> 01:01:45.313
He expresses himself with his face,

01:01:45.353 --> 01:01:46.214
with his way of being,

01:01:46.254 --> 01:01:48.696
with his playing style,

01:01:49.176 --> 01:01:50.357
with his body.

01:01:51.779 --> 01:01:54.181
Chaplin had a big problem and he solved it.

01:01:54.901 --> 01:01:56.443
simply by not speaking.

01:01:58.505 --> 01:01:59.025
It's decided,

01:01:59.886 --> 01:02:01.968
Chaplin will not succumb to the allure of modernity.

01:02:02.668 --> 01:02:03.168
For him,

01:02:03.209 --> 01:02:05.311
Talking pictures are just a passing fad.

01:02:06.071 --> 01:02:06.832
His new film,

01:02:07.433 --> 01:02:08.374
City Lights,

01:02:09.294 --> 01:02:09.875
will be mute.

01:02:11.175 --> 01:02:13.956
The first one took place in New York in January 1931.

01:02:14.956 --> 01:02:18.697
All of Hollywood traveled across the United States to discover the new Chaplin.

01:02:20.058 --> 01:02:22.599
The filmmaker invited another genius of his century,

01:02:23.499 --> 01:02:24.039
his new friend,

01:02:24.919 --> 01:02:26.320
Professor Albert Einstein.

01:02:30.681 --> 01:02:35.703
He was afraid that no one would come to see the film because no silent film had been released for years.

01:02:49.823 --> 01:02:54.178
The film is a love story between Charlie Chaplin and a little flower girl who has lost her sight.

01:02:55.121 --> 01:02:56.045
A poetic work,

01:02:56.085 --> 01:02:56.627
moving.

01:02:57.496 --> 01:02:58.477
and without any dialogue.

01:03:02.903 --> 01:03:03.403
In the end,

01:03:03.444 --> 01:03:06.168
It became the third biggest success of the year.

01:03:06.869 --> 01:03:08.251
Life magazine stated

01:03:09.232 --> 01:03:09.653
"The mute,

01:03:09.653 --> 01:03:11.054
if Chaplin directs,

01:03:11.555 --> 01:03:12.316
It's still gold.

01:03:29.608 --> 01:03:37.135
He provides the essential demonstration that one can remain what one wants to be.

01:03:38.316 --> 01:03:39.457
whatever the situation.

01:03:43.020 --> 01:03:50.306
I think everyone needs to have people remind us of that from time to time.

01:03:52.388 --> 01:03:54.090
Chaplin is once again making headlines.

01:03:54.570 --> 01:03:55.811
But this time, it's for his art.

01:03:57.228 --> 01:03:58.929
A success that, however, does not reassure him.

01:03:59.910 --> 01:04:00.410
Alone,

01:04:00.690 --> 01:04:02.952
tired and worried about the future of cinema,

01:04:03.912 --> 01:04:05.233
He needs to take a step back.

01:04:06.234 --> 01:04:08.995
He wants to escape the gloom and doom in Hollywood.

01:04:10.296 --> 01:04:11.297
So what is he going to do?

01:04:11.997 --> 01:04:14.799
How can we avoid being perceived as an anachronism?

01:04:14.939 --> 01:04:16.960
like a star from a bygone era,

01:04:17.641 --> 01:04:18.581
Completely off the mark?

01:04:21.163 --> 01:04:22.624
In February 1931,

01:04:23.576 --> 01:04:27.638
He will leave the United States and California to promote city lights in Europe.

01:04:28.698 --> 01:04:35.681
He has no idea yet how much this trip will change his worldview and give his art a second youth.

01:04:41.264 --> 01:04:42.024
First stop,

01:04:42.644 --> 01:04:43.245
England.

01:04:43.985 --> 01:04:47.586
Chaplin arrives in his hometown by train and finds his smile again.

01:04:48.367 --> 01:04:50.408
The prodigal son has returned.

01:04:51.168 --> 01:04:55.050
He enjoyed being appreciated by the people of the countries he visited.

01:04:55.090 --> 01:05:02.513
but he also liked being able to be received there as a prominent figure who could engage in dialogue with heads of state,

01:05:02.533 --> 01:05:03.614
intellectuals,

01:05:04.254 --> 01:05:05.154
other artists.

01:05:05.715 --> 01:05:06.215
In London,

01:05:06.795 --> 01:05:07.715
Winston Churchill,

01:05:08.136 --> 01:05:09.176
future Prime Minister

01:05:09.656 --> 01:05:10.657
asks to meet him.

01:05:11.417 --> 01:05:12.358
Mahatma Gandhi,

01:05:12.478 --> 01:05:15.039
came to negotiate India's independence with England,

01:05:15.599 --> 01:05:16.819
is also curious to see it.

01:05:18.440 --> 01:05:20.961
By positioning itself alongside the greats of the 20th century,

01:05:21.321 --> 01:05:24.122
He himself became a great figure of the 20th century.

01:05:26.502 --> 01:05:29.863
But beyond the popular jubilation and enthusiasm for his films,

01:05:31.003 --> 01:05:34.664
Chaplin realizes that the Great Depression has spread beyond the borders of America.

01:05:35.585 --> 01:05:36.485
Throughout Europe,

01:05:36.985 --> 01:05:40.426
People suffer and great nations retreat into themselves.

01:05:43.407 --> 01:05:45.887
He had become very aware of the global situation.

01:05:45.888 --> 01:05:46.249
And what he saw,

01:05:46.249 --> 01:05:47.688
The global situation was spiraling out of control.

01:05:48.128 --> 01:05:49.929
These were the dangers of nationalism.

01:05:51.030 --> 01:05:53.110
In March 1931,

01:05:53.111 --> 01:05:54.191
Chaplin arrives in Germany.

01:05:55.151 --> 01:05:59.033
And for the first time, he himself will be the target of this prevailing nationalism.

01:06:00.034 --> 01:06:00.554
In Berlin,

01:06:01.154 --> 01:06:02.555
The people gave him a triumphant welcome.

01:06:03.115 --> 01:06:05.456
But the Nazi press unleashed a torrent of attacks against him.

01:06:06.397 --> 01:06:07.918
Because he is a friend of Albert Einstein,

01:06:08.538 --> 01:06:09.218
He is said to be Jewish.

01:06:18.341 --> 01:06:23.365
"Does he leave the aforementioned lady to a sub-Gewandereux?"

01:06:23.385 --> 01:06:26.207
a tot-feind.

01:06:26.227 --> 01:06:31.552
In a dictionary they compiled to list a number of Jewish figures,

01:06:32.292 --> 01:06:33.593
They include Chaplin.

01:06:34.374 --> 01:06:35.095
Charlie Chaplin.

01:06:35.615 --> 01:06:36.876
This wiggling little Jew,

01:06:37.016 --> 01:06:40.999
boring and repugnant has become a myth of our time for Jewish families.

01:06:41.300 --> 01:06:42.240
That era is over.

01:06:42.781 --> 01:06:46.444
Upon discovering this text and its accompanying photo in this list of men to be eliminated,

01:06:47.352 --> 01:06:48.173
Chaplin is in shock,

01:06:49.273 --> 01:06:51.775
but he decides to leave his origins shrouded in doubt.

01:06:52.655 --> 01:06:53.316
He is not Jewish.

01:06:54.256 --> 01:06:56.177
but he will never try to deny it.

01:06:58.739 --> 01:07:05.283
He always said that denying being Jewish would be playing into the hands of anti-Semites.

01:07:07.044 --> 01:07:09.425
But the trip to Berlin holds another surprise for him.

01:07:10.466 --> 01:07:12.747
The press also mentions a striking resemblance.

01:07:12.787 --> 01:07:14.328
a strange coincidence of dates.

01:07:15.072 --> 01:07:17.333
with one of the rising figures of the nationalist right.

01:07:18.033 --> 01:07:19.493
When Chaplin arrived in Germany,

01:07:19.593 --> 01:07:23.074
There are small cartoon drawings that start immediately,

01:07:23.194 --> 01:07:25.475
even before Hitler seized power,

01:07:25.875 --> 01:07:26.795
comparing the two,

01:07:27.095 --> 01:07:30.616
the character of Charlot or the personality of Chaplin,

01:07:31.236 --> 01:07:31.736
And

01:07:31.757 --> 01:07:32.417
Adolf Hitler.

01:07:37.038 --> 01:07:38.678
They were born almost on the same day,

01:07:39.179 --> 01:07:39.799
the same year,

01:07:39.919 --> 01:07:41.079
in 1889.

01:07:41.799 --> 01:07:43.040
They had the same silhouette,

01:07:43.200 --> 01:07:44.140
the same moustache.

01:07:45.200 --> 01:07:49.383
There were newspapers that said Hitler got the idea for the moustache from Chaplin.

01:07:50.223 --> 01:07:51.244
And that made him very angry.

01:07:54.766 --> 01:07:56.067
Upon his return to the United States,

01:07:56.807 --> 01:07:58.368
Chaplin keeps thinking about all of this.

01:07:59.108 --> 01:07:59.969
He is no longer the same man.

01:08:00.489 --> 01:08:01.330
At 43 years old,

01:08:01.331 --> 01:08:02.790
He no longer just wants to make people laugh.

01:08:03.651 --> 01:08:06.412
But he understands that his films can also raise awareness.

01:08:08.093 --> 01:08:10.114
He witnessed the devastating effects of depression on nations.

01:08:11.035 --> 01:08:11.535
SO,

01:08:11.855 --> 01:08:12.636
His first target?

01:08:13.332 --> 01:08:14.353
It will be capitalism.

01:08:17.434 --> 01:08:17.934
In

01:08:19.736 --> 01:08:25.219
In 1936, he donned his Charlie Chaplin costume once again for a satire of the industrial world.

01:08:28.560 --> 01:08:29.281
Modern times,

01:08:29.341 --> 01:08:32.623
It's a film that denounces excessive consumerism.

01:08:33.483 --> 01:08:36.305
You don't see it as a light comedy,

01:08:36.725 --> 01:08:38.526
but like a true social film.

01:08:39.346 --> 01:08:40.067
And at the same time,

01:08:40.507 --> 01:08:41.287
It's very funny.

01:09:08.112 --> 01:09:10.553
It is a denunciation of everything that is happening today.

01:09:10.573 --> 01:09:11.614
The world is doomed.

01:09:11.934 --> 01:09:12.415
profit,

01:09:12.415 --> 01:09:12.915
profit,

01:09:12.916 --> 01:09:13.275
time,

01:09:13.275 --> 01:09:14.075
money,

01:09:14.576 --> 01:09:15.076
etc.

01:09:15.256 --> 01:09:17.217
It's beautifully done and then we finally have Paulette Godard.

01:09:19.679 --> 01:09:20.179
Paulette

01:09:20.579 --> 01:09:23.261
Godard, Charlie Chaplin's new partner.

01:09:24.089 --> 01:09:26.913
A 21-year-old actress whom he met upon her return from Europe,

01:09:27.693 --> 01:09:29.255
He gave her the lead female role.

01:09:33.660 --> 01:09:35.763
After a childhood quite similar to his own,

01:09:36.704 --> 01:09:37.445
separation,

01:09:37.765 --> 01:09:38.265
abandonment,

01:09:39.027 --> 01:09:42.171
So there was a kind of compassion and identification between them.

01:10:04.594 --> 01:10:06.457
This is his last silent film.

01:10:06.578 --> 01:10:09.764
It's very moving to see that he found love along the way.

01:10:10.926 --> 01:10:13.572
Moreover, for the first time, he is no longer going alone.

01:10:32.617 --> 01:10:35.999
But this is not the love story that the public will remember from modern times.

01:10:37.140 --> 01:10:41.143
Many people don't understand why Chaplin wanted to give a political dimension to his films.

01:10:42.504 --> 01:10:43.685
The reception in the dining room was mixed.

01:10:45.506 --> 01:10:46.707
However, this is only a first attempt.

01:10:48.088 --> 01:10:49.929
because he is already writing a new pamphlet.

01:10:51.371 --> 01:10:53.032
Adolf Hitler seized power in Germany,

01:10:54.193 --> 01:10:56.534
And while no one in Hollywood seems to be reacting,

01:10:57.555 --> 01:10:59.136
He intends to make a lasting impression.

01:11:00.477 --> 01:11:05.038
He will, in a way, settle his score with this evil twin.

01:11:08.479 --> 01:11:09.700
To portray his dictator,

01:11:10.500 --> 01:11:14.781
Chaplin drew inspiration from a series of photos in which Hitler practiced striking poses.

01:11:15.421 --> 01:11:20.463
Hitler took lessons with a teacher who taught him how to pose.

01:11:20.464 --> 01:11:21.703
to learn to express oneself.

01:11:22.243 --> 01:11:28.385
Chaplin immediately saw the strings behind what we might call Adolf Hitler's aura.

01:11:31.037 --> 01:11:31.717
He,
he saw the puppet,

01:11:31.797 --> 01:11:33.858
What?
He couldn't have imagined the horror that was about to unfold.

01:11:33.859 --> 01:11:34.998
Of course,
but he saw the puppet.

01:11:35.438 --> 01:11:36.719
So it was a source of inspiration.

01:11:37.319 --> 01:11:37.859
A madman like that.

01:11:39.179 --> 01:11:40.019
For the first time,

01:11:40.600 --> 01:11:42.520
Chaplin wrote a screenplay with dialogue.

01:11:43.400 --> 01:11:45.301
He devoted two whole years to it.

01:11:46.221 --> 01:11:48.062
He resigned himself to abandoning the art of silent film.

01:11:48.702 --> 01:11:49.442
out of necessity.

01:11:51.823 --> 01:11:53.803
Only because he wanted speeches in it.

01:11:54.603 --> 01:11:56.684
Speeches like those a politician would make.

01:11:56.804 --> 01:11:59.825
In September 1939...

01:12:01.021 --> 01:12:04.042
Chaplin began filming The Great Dictator in a very tense atmosphere.

01:12:05.323 --> 01:12:06.083
His brother Sidney,

01:12:06.123 --> 01:12:06.824
passing through,

01:12:07.364 --> 01:12:08.705
turns his images in color.

01:12:09.765 --> 01:12:10.385
At the same time,

01:12:10.386 --> 01:12:11.966
The situation is worsening in Europe.

01:12:12.786 --> 01:12:15.047
England and France have just declared war on Germany.

01:12:15.868 --> 01:12:18.089
The United States refuses to take part in this war.

01:12:18.889 --> 01:12:20.930
And Chaplin's project is causing a stir.

01:12:21.711 --> 01:12:22.291
In particular J.

01:12:22.571 --> 01:12:23.551
Edgar Hoover,

01:12:23.831 --> 01:12:26.933
The head of the FBI became the most powerful man in America.

01:12:27.537 --> 01:12:30.300
Hoover was like many American leaders of the time,

01:12:30.320 --> 01:12:35.026
In other words, he viewed it rather favorably.

01:12:35.887 --> 01:12:36.748
to begin with,

01:12:36.749 --> 01:12:37.129
I think,

01:12:37.129 --> 01:12:39.151
the rise of fascism in Germany,

01:12:39.191 --> 01:12:42.095
for the simple reason that it is the alternative to communism.

01:12:43.136 --> 01:12:43.456
SO,

01:12:43.456 --> 01:12:46.199
Tell the Jews in Hollywood to stop exasperating the Germans.

01:12:46.200 --> 01:12:47.401
This is not the right time.

01:12:59.369 --> 01:12:59.990
Hitler,
you know,

01:12:59.990 --> 01:13:01.050
He was very successful at the beginning.

01:13:01.630 --> 01:13:04.611
So he's a kind of hero for many people too.

01:13:05.791 --> 01:13:08.152
Chaplin was subjected to political and financial pressures.

01:13:09.632 --> 01:13:10.432
But it doesn't bend.

01:13:11.793 --> 01:13:12.433
On the contrary,

01:13:12.833 --> 01:13:14.434
He's regained the energy of his early days.

01:13:15.354 --> 01:13:16.374
He works day and night.

01:13:16.674 --> 01:13:18.295
Repeat each take dozens of times.

01:13:19.155 --> 01:13:20.675
The filming lasts more than 7 months.

01:13:23.356 --> 01:13:24.777
Charlie was a workaholic.

01:13:25.897 --> 01:13:29.538
It was not uncommon to stay 16 or 18 hours straight during filming.

01:13:31.699 --> 01:13:34.039
And then come back the next day to start all over again.

01:13:36.820 --> 01:13:38.040
Chaplin wants to be precise.

01:13:39.221 --> 01:13:42.482
Nazi propaganda films inspired his set designs.

01:13:43.182 --> 01:13:43.782
his costumes.

01:13:48.843 --> 01:13:49.423
More than ever,

01:13:50.124 --> 01:13:51.244
He wants to make this film a success.

01:13:53.224 --> 01:13:55.345
Aware that the stakes this time are not just cinematic.

01:13:55.373 --> 01:13:55.873
chart.

01:13:56.553 --> 01:14:00.634
His demands on his team and on himself are limitless.

01:14:02.015 --> 01:14:03.675
He's becoming this madman.

01:14:03.695 --> 01:14:05.616
He becomes this tyrant.

01:14:05.696 --> 01:14:07.036
He becomes this dictator,

01:14:07.316 --> 01:14:09.637
but with the little thing,

01:14:09.737 --> 01:14:11.678
the small gesture that changes everything.

01:14:15.859 --> 01:14:17.499
On October 15, 1940,

01:14:18.780 --> 01:14:20.880
The film is being screened in New York as a world premiere.

01:14:22.661 --> 01:14:23.381
But then again...

01:14:23.981 --> 01:14:26.803
Chaplin's political intent is not understood.

01:14:40.192 --> 01:14:41.053
In the final scene,

01:14:41.733 --> 01:14:45.956
Chaplin abandons his comedian's persona for a very committed personal speech.

01:14:52.889 --> 01:14:55.450
You are not machines,

01:14:55.451 --> 01:14:57.931
You are not cattle.

01:14:57.932 --> 01:14:59.252
You are men!

01:14:59.272 --> 01:15:00.773
You have love for humanity in your hearts.

01:15:00.774 --> 01:15:03.834
When Chaplin's fame overshadows his character,

01:15:04.694 --> 01:15:06.315
when Chaplin stopped playing the Tramp,

01:15:07.116 --> 01:15:10.197
when he becomes a politically engaged man who gives speeches,

01:15:10.797 --> 01:15:12.018
This is becoming problematic.

01:15:12.598 --> 01:15:15.459
because he is becoming a very polarizing figure in America.

01:15:15.479 --> 01:15:18.921
Let's do it for a world of reason!

01:15:19.581 --> 01:15:24.743
A world where science and progress will lead to the joy of all mankind.

01:15:24.763 --> 01:15:25.363
Soldiers,

01:15:25.364 --> 01:15:25.983
in the name of democracy,

01:15:25.984 --> 01:15:27.743
Let us all unite!

01:15:29.284 --> 01:15:31.605
The film has indeed been nominated for five Oscars,

01:15:32.445 --> 01:15:34.806
but few perceive its visionary aspect.

01:15:35.686 --> 01:15:36.186
Yet,

01:15:36.746 --> 01:15:38.347
in 1940,

01:15:38.348 --> 01:15:40.407
Hitler has already begun his destructive project.

01:15:43.188 --> 01:15:44.848
He had understood how to talk to people,

01:15:44.988 --> 01:15:46.629
how to tell them about the world.

01:15:47.457 --> 01:15:49.718
What he showed there was somewhat prophetic.

01:15:49.978 --> 01:15:51.419
what was going to happen with the Jews.

01:15:51.839 --> 01:15:55.361
He was the only one in Hollywood who released a film like that.

01:15:56.762 --> 01:15:59.003
He said that if he had known about the extermination camps,

01:15:59.624 --> 01:16:01.585
He could never have made a comedy out of it.

01:16:03.946 --> 01:16:04.687
After the war,

01:16:05.527 --> 01:16:07.728
It will be discovered that Hitler watched the dictator.

01:16:10.210 --> 01:16:13.852
Nazi archives reveal the order for a copy of the film.

01:16:16.377 --> 01:16:18.598
If the Nazi elite had one quality,

01:16:19.379 --> 01:16:20.539
It's because she loved the cinema.

01:16:23.281 --> 01:16:24.361
And even during the war,

01:16:24.722 --> 01:16:30.005
The Nazis found ways to obtain English and American films through neutral countries.

01:16:42.651 --> 01:16:45.313
The filmmaker has once again put a lot of himself into this film.

01:16:46.261 --> 01:16:47.362
Starting with his relationship,

01:16:48.462 --> 01:16:53.065
Paulette Godard left him during 1941 and divorced a year later.

01:16:54.305 --> 01:16:55.886
They hadn't seen each other for months.

01:16:58.187 --> 01:17:03.050
Those who collaborated with Chaplin know that he was totally absorbed in his work.

01:17:03.750 --> 01:17:04.271
And of course,

01:17:04.371 --> 01:17:07.052
His wives did not understand why he was completely neglecting them.

01:17:07.773 --> 01:17:10.774
His entire mind was focused on his work.

01:17:13.075 --> 01:17:13.776
Paulette Godard,

01:17:13.936 --> 01:17:14.417
Magnificent.

01:17:14.417 --> 01:17:15.577
I think it was...

01:17:16.057 --> 01:17:16.678
With my mother,

01:17:16.758 --> 01:17:18.419
It was also the end of his life.

01:17:18.979 --> 01:17:21.121
He had a tremendous love affair with her.

01:17:24.444 --> 01:17:26.486
This relationship truly humanized Chaplin.

01:17:26.766 --> 01:17:27.927
That prepared him for Ouna.

01:17:29.208 --> 01:17:29.968
Because two years later,

01:17:29.969 --> 01:17:30.869
at 54 years old,

01:17:31.510 --> 01:17:33.071
Chaplin makes a new acquaintance.

01:17:34.012 --> 01:17:34.572
Ouna O'Neill,

01:17:35.132 --> 01:17:36.694
the daughter of Nobel laureate Eugene O'Neill,

01:17:37.494 --> 01:17:40.797
a 17-year-old aspiring actress who was going through her first auditions at the time.

01:17:56.173 --> 01:17:58.255
When he met this other teenage girl,

01:17:58.655 --> 01:18:00.497
Everyone around him was very anxious.

01:18:02.860 --> 01:18:07.125
Everyone who knew about their romance believed it was still related to his attraction to young girls.

01:18:07.621 --> 01:18:08.021
After all,

01:18:08.021 --> 01:18:11.104
He was in his fifties and she was barely out of adolescence.

01:18:11.685 --> 01:18:14.767
It could only have been his obsessive sexual fantasy.

01:18:15.888 --> 01:18:16.589
But in reality,

01:18:16.689 --> 01:18:18.671
It became his greatest love story.

01:18:19.011 --> 01:18:24.896
They were passionately in love.

01:18:25.396 --> 01:18:28.079
And he, who was a soft touch,

01:18:28.519 --> 01:18:30.681
who collected women,

01:18:31.402 --> 01:18:35.125
It was truly an extraordinary romance.

01:18:37.257 --> 01:18:39.558
Chaplin married Una a few months after they met.

01:18:40.558 --> 01:18:43.440
But the beginning of this mayor's term is marred by a new sex scandal.

01:18:44.340 --> 01:18:44.980
The final straw.

01:18:46.601 --> 01:18:48.242
June 4, 1943,

01:18:49.002 --> 01:18:49.582
Joan Barry,

01:18:49.662 --> 01:18:50.323
23 years old,

01:18:50.943 --> 01:18:53.104
accuses Charlie Chaplin of being the father of her child.

01:18:53.804 --> 01:18:55.345
He was indeed impregnated by a man who then killed him.

01:18:55.373 --> 01:18:56.594
He had an affair with her,

01:18:57.335 --> 01:18:58.676
one year before meeting Ouna.

01:18:59.616 --> 01:19:00.917
But finding the young woman unstable,

01:19:01.558 --> 01:19:03.159
He had preferred to break up quickly.

01:19:04.960 --> 01:19:07.442
The whole story fell apart when Chaplin left her.

01:19:08.103 --> 01:19:10.445
That's when she started causing a lot of problems.

01:19:11.726 --> 01:19:13.287
Some time after their separation,

01:19:14.208 --> 01:19:16.730
Joan Barry breaks into Chaplin's home in the middle of the night.

01:19:17.770 --> 01:19:18.270
His son,

01:19:18.551 --> 01:19:19.051
Sidney,

01:19:19.872 --> 01:19:20.853
is present that evening.

01:19:22.493 --> 01:19:25.114
He goes upstairs and sees his father looking worried.

01:19:26.015 --> 01:19:27.035
He told him, "Dad,

01:19:27.135 --> 01:19:28.096
"Can I come see you?"

01:19:29.076 --> 01:19:30.677
And his father replied curtly, "No,

01:19:30.737 --> 01:19:31.237
Not now " .

01:19:31.977 --> 01:19:32.477
And then,

01:19:32.738 --> 01:19:37.019
He sees Joan Barry in her father's room with a gun in her hands.

01:19:40.241 --> 01:19:42.742
Joan Barry will be arrested twice for harassment.

01:19:44.563 --> 01:19:49.205
Chaplin thought this matter was buried until this paternity suit was filed.

01:19:51.165 --> 01:19:55.568
These accusations come at the same time as the official announcement of his marriage to Una.

01:19:56.529 --> 01:19:57.710
For many Americans,

01:19:58.190 --> 01:19:58.711
That's too much.

01:19:59.351 --> 01:20:02.593
Chaplin's attraction to young women is no longer tolerable.

01:20:04.094 --> 01:20:05.195
The American Legion,

01:20:05.235 --> 01:20:06.436
Catholic veterans,

01:20:06.756 --> 01:20:07.917
all feminist groups,

01:20:08.257 --> 01:20:12.581
I think they didn't really like this image of disgusting old men living with young women.

01:20:14.462 --> 01:20:15.723
For a segment of the population,

01:20:15.763 --> 01:20:18.265
He was nothing more than an aging womanizer.

01:20:18.945 --> 01:20:19.906
The John Barry case,

01:20:20.066 --> 01:20:22.247
Many people turned their backs on him because of that.

01:20:22.808 --> 01:20:23.468
And at the same time,

01:20:23.508 --> 01:20:24.889
He marries Una O'Neill,

01:20:24.929 --> 01:20:27.631
an 18-year-old girl when he is more than 5 years old.

01:20:29.973 --> 01:20:30.673
In Washington,

01:20:31.514 --> 01:20:32.515
A man rubs his hands together.

01:20:33.355 --> 01:20:34.396
For over 20 years,

01:20:34.436 --> 01:20:37.598
J.
Edgar Hoover is waiting for Chaplin's first misstep to bring him down.

01:20:38.659 --> 01:20:40.480
His file has grown thicker over the years,

01:20:41.261 --> 01:20:42.702
But he hasn't found anything illegal yet.

01:20:43.802 --> 01:20:45.103
So this John Barry affair,

01:20:46.044 --> 01:20:47.505
Hoover will take care of it personally.

01:20:50.897 --> 01:20:51.697
What's fascinating,

01:20:51.877 --> 01:20:53.998
This is how the FBI staged everything.

01:20:54.638 --> 01:20:56.359
John Berry did not want to file a complaint.

01:20:59.200 --> 01:21:05.083
J.
Edgar Hoover and essentially the entire American right wing used his story to demonize Chaplin.

01:21:07.343 --> 01:21:10.905
And the FBI realized that it could initiate numerous proceedings.

01:21:22.313 --> 01:21:24.274
February 15, 1944,

01:21:25.234 --> 01:21:29.036
Chaplin appears in court for the acknowledgment of Caroline's paternity.

01:21:29.736 --> 01:21:30.556
John Berry's daughter.

01:21:32.517 --> 01:21:36.539
Chaplin's lawyer presents the results of a blood test that proves he is not the father.

01:21:37.979 --> 01:21:39.940
But the FBI is in control of the situation.

01:21:41.801 --> 01:21:42.601
That's huge.

01:21:43.021 --> 01:21:45.863
The reason is that it was the FBI itself that appointed the judge.

01:21:46.723 --> 01:21:47.123
And so,

01:21:47.123 --> 01:21:48.944
The blood tests were rejected.

01:21:50.204 --> 01:21:51.445
Chaplin is found guilty.

01:21:52.285 --> 01:21:56.468
And he is ordered to pay alimony to John Barry's daughter until she turns 21.

01:22:00.211 --> 01:22:00.951
But for Hoover,

01:22:01.812 --> 01:22:02.713
That is not enough.

01:22:03.593 --> 01:22:06.235
The head of the FBI then launched another procedure.

01:22:07.056 --> 01:22:11.199
He found a very old federal law that prohibits a man from taking a woman on a trip.

01:22:11.719 --> 01:22:12.660
for immoral purposes,

01:22:13.140 --> 01:22:13.720
the manact.

01:22:14.681 --> 01:22:16.843
Because he took John Barry on vacation to New York,

01:22:17.323 --> 01:22:18.124
Chaplin risks

01:22:18.584 --> 01:22:19.585
23 years in prison.

01:22:21.641 --> 01:22:23.542
The prosecutor was horrible to him.

01:22:24.143 --> 01:22:26.104
by portraying him as a sexual predator,

01:22:26.644 --> 01:22:27.445
like a monster.

01:22:28.545 --> 01:22:30.806
They photographed him while they were taking his fingerprints.

01:22:32.327 --> 01:22:34.008
This photo appears in numerous newspapers.

01:22:34.769 --> 01:22:37.710
Everything is being used to make him appear guilty.

01:22:39.491 --> 01:22:40.952
But the jurors are not fooled.

01:22:41.753 --> 01:22:43.854
On April 4, 1944,

01:22:44.694 --> 01:22:45.615
They acquit Chaplin.

01:22:47.136 --> 01:22:47.636
Yet,

01:22:48.336 --> 01:22:49.557
Hoover doesn't let go of his prey.

01:22:50.301 --> 01:22:54.123
And part of the conservative press remains in the pay of the FBI.

01:22:56.163 --> 01:23:00.945
They spent their time giving small pieces of information to journalists who had rallied to their cause.

01:23:01.345 --> 01:23:02.266
like Hedda Hopper,

01:23:02.866 --> 01:23:03.826
which was definitely on the right.

01:23:05.447 --> 01:23:06.067
Hedda Hopper,

01:23:06.728 --> 01:23:10.129
who wrote for the tabloids at the time,

01:23:10.729 --> 01:23:12.330
She's the one who started the rumors.

01:23:12.990 --> 01:23:15.591
Feminist leagues are collecting signatures for petitions across the country.

01:23:16.372 --> 01:23:19.933
They hope for Chaplin's deportation on grounds of moral turpitude.

01:23:20.657 --> 01:23:24.939
Immigration services have informed me that they are investigating all aspects of his presence here.

01:23:25.999 --> 01:23:27.520
An article signed

01:23:27.920 --> 01:23:28.620
"Eda Hopper",

01:23:29.220 --> 01:23:31.141
but which seems clearly dictated by Hoover.

01:23:31.962 --> 01:23:33.062
The term "deportation"

01:23:33.102 --> 01:23:35.403
is a term that is taken up by Hoover.

01:23:36.283 --> 01:23:36.624
Besides,

01:23:36.624 --> 01:23:39.084
He very often threatens people with deportation.

01:23:39.365 --> 01:23:41.145
We know what deportation means.

01:23:41.906 --> 01:23:44.086
The symbol is terrifying.

01:23:45.187 --> 01:23:46.788
Chaplin is under attack from all sides.

01:23:47.088 --> 01:23:48.408
But instead of keeping a low profile,

01:23:48.848 --> 01:23:50.209
He responds with provocation.

01:23:50.745 --> 01:23:51.586
With a new film,

01:23:52.066 --> 01:23:52.707
Mr. Verdoux.

01:23:54.369 --> 01:23:57.371
In it, he plays a woman-killer inspired by the French serial killer.

01:23:57.752 --> 01:23:58.252
Landru.

01:24:13.311 --> 01:24:13.971
Once again,

01:24:13.972 --> 01:24:14.891
He found it amusing.

01:24:15.632 --> 01:24:16.472
by playing Landru,

01:24:16.552 --> 01:24:20.814
the French bluebeard who married wealthy widows and murdered them.

01:24:20.815 --> 01:24:22.875
As a mask artist,

01:24:24.035 --> 01:24:25.896
Doesn't the world encourage it?

01:24:25.897 --> 01:24:30.298
Isn't this building weapons of destruction for the sole purpose of disguise?

01:24:30.299 --> 01:24:36.781
Isn't that extinguishing women and children into tiny pieces?

01:24:36.782 --> 01:24:37.361
It's more Chaplin.

01:24:37.441 --> 01:24:39.602
What?
The little vagabond allowed him to get away with all sorts of things.

01:24:40.014 --> 01:24:40.655
As soon as he leaves him,

01:24:40.695 --> 01:24:43.597
He becomes more like everyone else.

01:24:43.598 --> 01:24:44.298
One could say,

01:24:44.538 --> 01:24:45.118
Oh,
Mr.

01:24:45.118 --> 01:24:45.459
Verdoux,

01:24:45.459 --> 01:24:46.239
What an excellent film.

01:24:47.380 --> 01:24:55.727
But is this really reasonable for a man who has just come through a difficult paternity suit and who has a whole host of problems with women?

01:24:56.528 --> 01:24:59.430
To play a Bluebeard who kills his wives for their money?

01:25:08.922 --> 01:25:11.383
I'm going to lose my mind.

01:25:11.403 --> 01:25:13.324
Nevertheless,

01:25:13.364 --> 01:25:17.287
leaving behind this noise of earthly existence,

01:25:17.347 --> 01:25:23.370
I have to say that I will see you all very soon.

01:25:24.571 --> 01:25:28.393
The attack was clumsy and the result catastrophic for Chaplin.

01:25:29.373 --> 01:25:30.854
The film was a commercial failure.

01:25:30.974 --> 01:25:33.236
censored and banned in several states.

01:25:35.857 --> 01:25:37.098
It was an organized boycott.

01:25:37.874 --> 01:25:42.175
It was the beginning of the Cold War and there was a crusade against communism in the United States.

01:25:43.976 --> 01:25:47.217
This was the missing piece for Hoover to deliver the fatal blow.

01:25:48.317 --> 01:25:49.537
At the end of the 1940s,

01:25:50.218 --> 01:25:54.539
The hunt for communists has just been officially launched by Senator McCarthy.

01:26:06.250 --> 01:26:08.652
In this climate of paranoia and inquisition,

01:26:09.653 --> 01:26:12.455
Chaplin's work then takes on a completely different meaning.

01:26:13.596 --> 01:26:20.882
He had spoken out against what he saw as the excesses of industrial capitalism in modern times.

01:26:21.783 --> 01:26:22.584
Hoover is looking for,

01:26:23.164 --> 01:26:29.370
He searches and eventually finds a record of a speech in which Chaplin clearly supports the Russians.

01:26:32.973 --> 01:26:34.494
1942.

01:26:34.694 --> 01:26:40.777
He was asked to replace the Soviet ambassador in San Francisco at a large gathering in

01:26:42.899 --> 01:26:47.041
1942. The goal was to push the government to open a second front.

01:26:50.703 --> 01:26:53.305
He began his speech by saying to the audience

01:26:53.885 --> 01:26:54.445
"comrades".

01:26:56.306 --> 01:26:56.806
This moment,

01:26:56.847 --> 01:26:58.107
when he said "comrades",

01:26:58.468 --> 01:26:59.848
He was bound to be criticized.

01:27:01.109 --> 01:27:02.530
Hoover thinks he's onto something.

01:27:03.466 --> 01:27:04.546
Chaplin is being bugged,

01:27:05.207 --> 01:27:06.687
His entourage is also being questioned.

01:27:08.548 --> 01:27:09.048
" THE

01:27:09.428 --> 01:27:15.550
The FBI came to see Sam Goldwyn and asked him if Chaplin was a communist.

01:27:17.911 --> 01:27:18.751
He replied

01:27:19.711 --> 01:27:20.952
"Charlie, a communist?"

01:27:23.352 --> 01:27:26.053
He's the only true capitalist I know!

01:27:30.223 --> 01:27:31.163
It was ridiculous.

01:27:31.643 --> 01:27:32.143
Obviously,

01:27:32.323 --> 01:27:34.104
He was closer to socialism.

01:27:34.324 --> 01:27:34.924
from the left,

01:27:35.225 --> 01:27:36.465
like many artists.

01:27:37.105 --> 01:27:38.766
But he was not a communist at all.

01:27:39.266 --> 01:27:39.967
Absolutely not.

01:27:41.907 --> 01:27:44.488
Nothing, therefore, confirms a communist commitment.

01:27:45.589 --> 01:27:46.889
But despite the lack of evidence,

01:27:47.650 --> 01:27:51.611
All these years of anti-Chaplin propaganda are beginning to bear fruit.

01:27:52.752 --> 01:27:53.792
In 1950,

01:27:53.812 --> 01:27:54.472
in the United States,

01:27:55.113 --> 01:27:56.173
We don't talk about these films anymore.

01:27:56.893 --> 01:27:58.374
Forget the genius of the 7th art.

01:27:59.235 --> 01:28:00.316
For Puritan America,

01:28:00.996 --> 01:28:04.299
Chaplin is now nothing more than an old man with dangerous political ideas.

01:28:04.759 --> 01:28:06.100
He was accused of being a communist.

01:28:06.481 --> 01:28:07.822
And if you go to see a communist,

01:28:07.823 --> 01:28:08.903
It means you're a supporter.

01:28:08.963 --> 01:28:09.964
Otherwise, you yourself are a communist.

01:28:10.504 --> 01:28:12.866
So it was the worst accusation in America.

01:28:17.050 --> 01:28:23.315
He senses that a kind of mistrust and rejection is beginning to manifest itself.

01:28:24.716 --> 01:28:26.818
All of Hollywood found him a bit tiresome.

01:28:27.578 --> 01:28:32.479
He became persona non grata and no one came to visit him anymore.

01:28:33.860 --> 01:28:35.780
So Chaplin gradually cut himself off from the world.

01:28:36.621 --> 01:28:40.542
He spends his days in his villa and seeks comfort from his family.

01:28:41.282 --> 01:28:43.062
his wife Ouna and their children.

01:28:52.005 --> 01:28:52.505
A day,

01:28:52.685 --> 01:28:54.285
We were walking towards the tennis court,

01:28:55.046 --> 01:28:55.846
Just the two of them.

01:28:56.618 --> 01:28:58.540
We talked about everything and nothing,

01:28:59.580 --> 01:29:01.042
and at one point he told me

01:29:01.742 --> 01:29:07.226
"I never knew what love was until I met this woman."

01:29:08.307 --> 01:29:09.048
It just came out like that.

01:29:09.948 --> 01:29:10.929
Very impressive.

01:29:15.994 --> 01:29:17.855
She was like a surrogate mother to him.

01:29:18.276 --> 01:29:18.916
his sister.

01:29:19.196 --> 01:29:19.537
In addition,

01:29:19.537 --> 01:29:24.301
Ouna somewhat corresponded to his ideal of a slightly fragile woman,

01:29:25.342 --> 01:29:28.625
erased at the same time with a great deal of character.

01:29:28.965 --> 01:29:29.465
But here's the thing,

01:29:30.146 --> 01:29:33.449
It was a complete and mutual idyll.

01:29:34.170 --> 01:29:34.670
Lover,

01:29:35.311 --> 01:29:36.472
but withdrawn into himself,

01:29:37.192 --> 01:29:38.934
in the melancholy of a bygone glory.

01:29:39.690 --> 01:29:42.132
Chaplin would then create his final masterpiece,

01:29:42.733 --> 01:29:43.513
The Footlights,

01:29:44.274 --> 01:29:46.095
the story of a fallen musical artist,

01:29:47.016 --> 01:29:49.198
his most autobiographical film.

01:29:52.260 --> 01:29:53.081
For the first time,

01:29:53.101 --> 01:29:57.164
He reunites the alcoholic artist with the young and beautiful dancer,

01:29:57.825 --> 01:30:00.947
which obviously symbolizes the relationship of his own parents.

01:30:03.369 --> 01:30:06.572
But her imagination transforms it into a love relationship.

01:30:06.752 --> 01:30:07.993
happy and generous.

01:30:10.718 --> 01:30:12.379
He entrusted the female role to Claire Bloom.

01:30:13.400 --> 01:30:16.822
a young actress chosen for her resemblance to the two women in his life,

01:30:17.463 --> 01:30:18.924
his mother and Una.

01:30:23.807 --> 01:30:24.568
At that time,

01:30:24.728 --> 01:30:25.188
One and I,

01:30:25.188 --> 01:30:26.469
We were very similar.

01:30:27.650 --> 01:30:28.991
And during the filming of the movie,

01:30:29.231 --> 01:30:30.732
We were often mistaken for each other.

01:30:32.433 --> 01:30:34.094
Chaplin wants to bring his story together.

01:30:34.895 --> 01:30:35.475
his family,

01:30:36.255 --> 01:30:37.156
to bring their lives together,

01:30:38.097 --> 01:30:39.177
his children Geraldine,

01:30:39.298 --> 01:30:39.798
Michael...

01:30:40.058 --> 01:30:42.600
And Josephine even makes an appearance.

01:30:48.244 --> 01:30:49.664
I wanted to tell everyone at school,

01:30:49.725 --> 01:30:51.386
But I made films.

01:30:52.286 --> 01:30:57.390
It's like following in your father's footsteps.

01:30:57.391 --> 01:31:02.353
There's something archetypal about it that really made it a magical moment for me.

01:31:02.853 --> 01:31:04.274
And in the role of the young suitor,

01:31:05.275 --> 01:31:06.396
We also find Sidney,

01:31:07.256 --> 01:31:09.578
the second son born from his marriage to Lita Gray.

01:31:24.986 --> 01:31:25.486
Finally,

01:31:26.167 --> 01:31:30.109
He chose the London of his childhood as the setting for his story.

01:31:30.710 --> 01:31:32.110
reconstructed exactly as it was.

01:31:33.071 --> 01:31:33.651
In one film,

01:31:34.532 --> 01:31:36.933
Chaplin reviews all the major themes of his life.

01:31:40.515 --> 01:31:43.936
It's a wonderful exploration of her feelings.

01:31:44.336 --> 01:31:45.076
from his family,

01:31:45.216 --> 01:31:46.657
feelings from his family

01:31:46.977 --> 01:31:47.877
of its history,

01:31:48.177 --> 01:31:49.717
of what he remembers of London.

01:31:50.198 --> 01:31:51.338
And not always good times.

01:31:52.919 --> 01:31:54.459
It's a very,

01:31:54.499 --> 01:31:55.019
very rich.

01:31:56.580 --> 01:31:57.640
A final film, a testament to his life.

01:31:58.460 --> 01:31:59.661
almost prophetic,

01:32:00.481 --> 01:32:03.702
He doesn't yet know that this will be the last one filmed in the United States.

01:32:12.130 --> 01:32:13.691
In September 1952,

01:32:14.631 --> 01:32:16.191
Chaplin sets sail for England.

01:32:17.892 --> 01:32:23.433
This is the first planned stop on a long promotional tour in Europe for Limelight.

01:32:23.933 --> 01:32:28.115
Because the film was set in London and things were going badly in the United States,

01:32:28.615 --> 01:32:30.335
The first one was supposed to take place in London.

01:32:31.556 --> 01:32:35.277
He knows that the FBI is watching him and that the IRS is looking for him.

01:32:36.017 --> 01:32:37.697
So, out of fear of not being able to leave,

01:32:38.458 --> 01:32:40.138
He did not announce the date of his departure.

01:32:40.758 --> 01:32:43.661
And he boards the Queen Elizabeth in anonymity.

01:32:46.643 --> 01:32:48.785
His wife and children are already on board.

01:32:49.726 --> 01:32:53.289
He remained hidden in his cabin until the ship left the port.

01:32:54.650 --> 01:32:55.391
But in Washington,

01:32:56.331 --> 01:32:58.333
Hoover has no intention of detaining him.

01:32:59.114 --> 01:32:59.714
On the contrary,

01:33:00.635 --> 01:33:01.716
informed of his departure,

01:33:02.677 --> 01:33:03.758
He's going to set a trap for him.

01:33:07.128 --> 01:33:08.149
On the second day at sea,

01:33:09.309 --> 01:33:11.571
Chaplin receives a message from immigration services.

01:33:15.573 --> 01:33:19.375
His visa to return to the United States has just been refused.

01:33:23.117 --> 01:33:24.598
Charlie was not officially banned,

01:33:24.878 --> 01:33:26.459
He couldn't stop her from coming back.

01:33:27.039 --> 01:33:29.921
But they created a situation where if he wanted a new visa,

01:33:30.021 --> 01:33:32.742
He had to start all the official procedures again.

01:33:34.223 --> 01:33:35.464
Hoover's trap is simple.

01:33:36.368 --> 01:33:37.329
To obtain this visa,

01:33:38.370 --> 01:33:40.992
Chaplin will have to undergo questioning by the FBI.

01:33:42.053 --> 01:33:42.753
If he refuses,

01:33:43.374 --> 01:33:44.355
He cannot come back.

01:33:45.195 --> 01:33:45.776
If he accepts,

01:33:46.437 --> 01:33:48.318
He will once again have to expose his private life.

01:33:48.598 --> 01:33:49.159
in broad daylight.

01:33:51.761 --> 01:33:52.642
During his absence,

01:33:52.742 --> 01:33:56.365
They interviewed all the women who had had sexual relations with him.

01:33:56.905 --> 01:33:58.767
with the aim of attacking his moral life.

01:34:00.028 --> 01:34:02.971
They hoped he would come back and contradict himself.

01:34:03.311 --> 01:34:04.552
in order to be able to indict him.

01:34:05.196 --> 01:34:06.576
But he wasn't stupid enough for that.

01:34:09.277 --> 01:34:12.058
The Queen Elizabeth arrives in England on September 23rd.

01:34:12.738 --> 01:34:15.559
He presents himself to the English people as a good family man.

01:34:16.720 --> 01:34:17.560
To begin with,

01:34:18.180 --> 01:34:21.001
The triumphant welcome made him forget his American dispute.

01:34:24.142 --> 01:34:27.743
There was immense love and a lot of support for him.

01:34:28.763 --> 01:34:30.664
It was packed with people applauding.

01:34:34.164 --> 01:34:36.807
It was truly one of the most moving scenes I've ever seen.

01:34:37.407 --> 01:34:39.469
Everyone moved aside as he passed.

01:34:40.610 --> 01:34:42.471
All those wonderful Londoners who told him

01:34:42.811 --> 01:34:43.712
"Hello Charlie"

01:34:44.132 --> 01:34:44.632
Or

01:34:44.693 --> 01:34:45.574
"Welcome Charlie".

01:34:47.455 --> 01:34:51.539
But the British already know that the United States has refused to give him his return visa.

01:34:52.840 --> 01:34:53.340
SO,

01:34:53.780 --> 01:34:55.682
at the press conference for the film,

01:34:56.422 --> 01:34:58.364
The filmmaker will have to react.

01:34:59.045 --> 01:35:00.226
The English gave him a warm welcome.

01:35:00.346 --> 01:35:01.006
as always.

01:35:01.326 --> 01:35:02.968
But they were also on the defensive.

01:35:03.308 --> 01:35:05.670
They were very shocked, even in Parliament.

01:35:06.010 --> 01:35:08.312
We talked about how the Americans treated him.

01:35:22.121 --> 01:35:25.183
Chaplin

01:35:25.303 --> 01:35:27.025
tries to get out of it with a pirouette.

01:35:28.025 --> 01:35:30.767
He was very careful and didn't say anything "bad".

01:35:30.927 --> 01:35:31.868
about America.

01:35:33.028 --> 01:35:34.229
And he is right to be cautious.

01:35:35.189 --> 01:35:36.209
because from the moment of his arrival,

01:35:37.190 --> 01:35:38.590
British intelligence services,

01:35:39.030 --> 01:35:39.530
MI5,

01:35:40.511 --> 01:35:43.712
They begin to monitor him and report to the FBI.

01:35:45.213 --> 01:35:52.636
His file was opened in 1952 when the FBI sent a message to MI5 requesting that one of us closely monitor this man.

01:35:53.396 --> 01:35:53.976
Charlie Chaplin.

01:35:55.837 --> 01:35:57.778
MI5 reacted at the heart of it all.

01:35:58.438 --> 01:36:00.039
When the FBI asks for something,

01:36:00.059 --> 01:36:01.359
MI5 responds, "Yes,

01:36:01.419 --> 01:36:01.800
chief !

01:36:01.800 --> 01:36:02.440
Yes,
chef!

01:36:03.396 --> 01:36:06.597
Chaplin therefore understands that he is not necessarily welcome in England.

01:36:07.558 --> 01:36:09.719
And the news from the United States isn't good either.

01:36:10.859 --> 01:36:13.300
His film is hardly being shown anywhere.

01:36:22.884 --> 01:36:25.085
The film was not released in major cities.

01:36:25.926 --> 01:36:26.426
as

01:36:26.566 --> 01:36:27.286
San Francisco,

01:36:28.787 --> 01:36:29.387
New York,

