Because these were considered anti-American activities,

01:36:35.111 --> 01:36:35.771
as they say.

01:36:38.013 --> 01:36:39.354
Chaplin has to make a decision.

01:36:40.695 --> 01:36:41.696
And he will choose exile.

01:36:42.896 --> 01:36:44.598
He will not return to the United States.

01:36:47.020 --> 01:36:50.362
He then did everything he could to permanently sever ties with that country.

01:36:51.583 --> 01:36:52.203
The priority?

01:36:53.064 --> 01:36:54.885
Finding a new home for his family.

01:36:57.187 --> 01:36:58.168
He travels around Europe.

01:36:58.840 --> 01:37:01.261
and eventually discovers a splendid manor house in Switzerland,

01:37:01.941 --> 01:37:02.802
on the shores of Lake Geneva.

01:37:05.623 --> 01:37:09.184
It is here at the Banque mansion that Charlie Chaplin will continue his life.

01:37:09.584 --> 01:37:11.025
But what is his state of mind?

01:37:11.505 --> 01:37:13.546
He was the one who decided not to return to the United States.

01:37:14.026 --> 01:37:15.787
But he knows very well that he had no choice.

01:37:16.207 --> 01:37:19.869
J.
Edgar Hoover is already presenting his departure as his greatest trophy.

01:37:20.409 --> 01:37:22.810
So,
will Chaplin accept this change of life?

01:37:23.290 --> 01:37:25.691
He, who has just experienced the glamour of Hollywood for 40 years,

01:37:26.151 --> 01:37:27.972
finally decides to cut himself off from the world.

01:37:28.440 --> 01:37:30.441
This could be seen as an early retirement,

01:37:30.861 --> 01:37:32.622
But Chaplin has no intention of disappearing.

01:37:33.082 --> 01:37:35.383
even though for the moment his main concern,

01:37:35.583 --> 01:37:36.283
It's his family.

01:37:36.864 --> 01:37:37.364
Ouna,

01:37:37.444 --> 01:37:38.044
his wife,

01:37:38.544 --> 01:37:40.285
is pregnant with their fifth child.

01:37:54.171 --> 01:37:56.612
I had my father bring us here.

01:37:57.028 --> 01:37:58.629
To see the house,

01:37:58.729 --> 01:37:59.609
What is the house?

01:38:00.770 --> 01:38:02.131
And it was impressive.

01:38:07.714 --> 01:38:09.635
The sale went very quickly, as is often the case.

01:38:09.895 --> 01:38:11.216
Everything that Mr.

01:38:11.456 --> 01:38:11.956
Chaplin,

01:38:12.096 --> 01:38:12.837
It was fate.

01:38:18.099 --> 01:38:20.040
Chaplin thus found a home for his family.

01:38:20.801 --> 01:38:23.262
He now has to repatriate all his belongings left in Hollywood.

01:38:27.204 --> 01:38:27.765
Basically,

01:38:28.165 --> 01:38:30.626
They had only left with the essentials for their vacation.

01:38:30.766 --> 01:38:31.266
Nothing more.

01:38:32.788 --> 01:38:33.968
They had left all their possessions behind.

01:38:34.669 --> 01:38:37.490
They didn't know if they were going to be confiscated or what was going to happen.

01:38:39.892 --> 01:38:41.513
He can no longer leave.

01:38:42.513 --> 01:38:43.013
SO,

01:38:43.314 --> 01:38:46.656
He sends Una to Los Angeles to manage their assets.

01:38:48.377 --> 01:38:48.957
Before leaving,

01:38:48.997 --> 01:38:50.718
She put everything under her own name.

01:38:50.878 --> 01:38:52.699
She sold the house.

01:38:52.819 --> 01:38:53.500
the furniture,

01:38:53.520 --> 01:38:54.020
All of that.

01:38:58.201 --> 01:39:00.403
Ouna had to go through a very difficult time.

01:39:01.084 --> 01:39:03.266
She was forced to surrender her American passport.

01:39:05.047 --> 01:39:06.769
To accompany her husband to the very end,

01:39:07.730 --> 01:39:09.872
Ouna agrees to take British citizenship.

01:39:11.173 --> 01:39:12.875
At the end of 1954,

01:39:14.116 --> 01:39:18.600
All of Charlie Chaplin's films were repatriated to London and his fortune to Switzerland.

01:39:19.597 --> 01:39:20.438
At 65,

01:39:21.098 --> 01:39:22.119
He is starting a new life.

01:39:24.981 --> 01:39:26.402
He reconnects with his brother Sidney.

01:39:26.962 --> 01:39:28.743
