01:40:59.669 --> 01:41:03.210
He was still afraid of becoming poor again despite having a considerable fortune.

01:41:04.190 --> 01:41:05.030
On two occasions,

01:41:05.871 --> 01:41:07.991
Chaplin is trying to make a comeback.

01:41:08.671 --> 01:41:09.972
In 1957,

01:41:10.512 --> 01:41:12.232
He is writing and directing a new film.

01:41:13.113 --> 01:41:14.053
A king in New York.

01:41:15.081 --> 01:41:19.164
An anti-American diatribe that will never be shown in the United States.

01:41:37.016 --> 01:41:41.279
This film will primarily result in the return of wiretapping.

01:41:42.460 --> 01:41:43.701
openness to tenacious hatred,

01:41:44.525 --> 01:41:48.667
The FBI even manages to convince the Swiss to keep an eye on Chaplin.

01:41:51.508 --> 01:41:53.409
The Swiss government bugged his house.

01:41:53.709 --> 01:41:55.170
There was a microphone in the phone.

01:41:58.691 --> 01:42:02.393
The Swiss secret services were terribly cooperative with the FBI.

01:42:02.993 --> 01:42:04.834
They were sending information constantly.

01:42:05.434 --> 01:42:07.395
They were watched until the very end.

01:42:07.396 --> 01:42:12.077
That is to say, we have records up to 1978.

01:42:19.857 --> 01:42:21.297
Thank you.

01:42:23.518 --> 01:42:24.778
Chaplin is filming one last movie.

01:42:25.419 --> 01:42:26.539
in 1967,

01:42:27.399 --> 01:42:28.379
The Countess of Hong Kong.

01:42:29.680 --> 01:42:31.820
Two stars have agreed to join him in his project.

01:42:32.720 --> 01:42:34.901
Sophia Loren and Marlon Brando.

01:42:36.562 --> 01:42:42.063
For him, it was surely a kind of return to his youth from the good old days.

01:42:42.663 --> 01:42:46.724
But it's also the pleasure of working with the biggest stars of the time,

01:42:47.044 --> 01:42:49.365
Brando and Sophia Loren.

01:42:49.545 --> 01:42:51.968
They immediately agreed to work with Charlie Chaplin.

01:42:52.769 --> 01:42:53.970
But the filming goes badly.

01:42:54.931 --> 01:42:56.393
Chaplin and Brando did not get along.

01:42:57.494 --> 01:42:59.336
They will put on a good show until the end of the film.

01:43:00.337 --> 01:43:01.638
but they will no longer speak to each other.

01:43:07.084 --> 01:43:11.169
They were two great men who were not meant to work together.

01:43:12.955 --> 01:43:13.936
The film is a failure.

01:43:15.116 --> 01:43:15.616
Yet,

01:43:16.336 --> 01:43:17.216
Chaplin persists.

01:43:18.317 --> 01:43:25.879
He locks himself in his office to write new screenplays and spends entire days at the piano reworking the music for his films.

01:43:33.301 --> 01:43:35.322
Recomposing film scores,

01:43:35.323 --> 01:43:35.763
at that time,

