All,

01:48:31.670 --> 01:48:32.990
with the exception of his childhood.

01:48:33.390 --> 01:48:35.131
You had a rather unhappy childhood.

01:49:08.851 --> 01:49:12.253
This is about the Kni Circus's visit to Vevey.

01:49:13.334 --> 01:49:15.215
In October 1977,

01:49:16.176 --> 01:49:18.317
while he hardly moves from his armchair,

01:49:19.518 --> 01:49:22.540
He insists once again that we take him there.

01:49:24.581 --> 01:49:26.562
It was clear he wasn't doing well.

01:49:27.142 --> 01:49:27.763
But still,

01:49:28.143 --> 01:49:30.024
He absolutely wanted to see the show.

01:49:30.025 --> 01:49:30.825
And we said,

01:49:31.065 --> 01:49:32.045
He is so tired,

01:49:32.146 --> 01:49:33.406
But he wanted to come to the circus.

01:49:33.446 --> 01:49:33.946
absolutely.

01:49:38.791 --> 01:49:39.891
We,
during the show,

01:49:39.911 --> 01:49:40.372
always,

01:49:40.372 --> 01:49:43.532
Flowers were brought for Onin.

01:49:44.173 --> 01:49:44.554
and him,

01:49:44.554 --> 01:49:45.413
He was laughing like a madman,

01:49:45.453 --> 01:49:46.013
and every year,

01:49:46.053 --> 01:49:46.553
We did that.

01:49:46.613 --> 01:49:47.554
And he was still laughing.

01:49:53.936 --> 01:49:54.596
It was wonderful.

01:49:54.616 --> 01:49:55.376
because the Knin,

01:49:55.377 --> 01:49:58.517
They were expected at intermission or at the end of the show in their caravan.

01:49:58.737 --> 01:49:59.098
Sometimes,

01:49:59.098 --> 01:50:00.718
He stayed until two o'clock in the morning.

01:50:00.798 --> 01:50:01.518
the following day,

01:50:01.778 --> 01:50:03.378
to talk with the clowns,

01:50:03.418 --> 01:50:04.279
with the artists,

01:50:04.319 --> 01:50:05.019
He loved it.

01:50:17.443 --> 01:50:20.544
He went very far back into his childhood.

01:50:20.884 --> 01:50:21.784
when he went to the circus.

01:50:29.047 --> 01:50:30.247
In the twilight of his life,

01:50:31.387 --> 01:50:33.208
Chaplin did not forget the magic of the circus.

01:50:34.448 --> 01:50:37.129
But he also retained some less happy childhood memories.

01:50:38.169 --> 01:50:38.609
Christmas,

01:50:38.609 --> 01:50:39.230
For example.

01:50:40.390 --> 01:50:40.890
A date,

01:50:41.510 --> 01:50:43.051
a party he never could stand.

01:50:43.795 --> 01:50:44.316
He didn't like it.

01:50:44.336 --> 01:50:44.656
No.

01:50:44.656 --> 01:50:45.356
It depressed him.

01:50:45.757 --> 01:50:47.478
I'm thinking about that.

01:50:47.479 --> 01:50:49.340
There were too many memories at Christmas.

01:50:50.841 --> 01:50:52.122
He must have gone through something terrible.

01:50:53.383 --> 01:50:53.883
the child.

01:50:54.604 --> 01:50:55.685
When he lived in London,

01:50:56.426 --> 01:50:58.327
Chaplin was not entitled to a dinner,

01:50:58.367 --> 01:50:59.088
nor to gifts.

01:51:00.449 --> 01:51:04.773
He likes to remind his children that his only pleasure that evening was an orange.

01:51:05.133 --> 01:51:06.634
I felt we received far too many gifts.

01:51:06.934 --> 01:51:07.675
thanks to my mother.

01:51:07.975 --> 01:51:08.936
It had become a bit,

01:51:08.996 --> 01:51:09.317
I believe,

01:51:09.317 --> 01:51:10.878
It's a myth to say...

01:51:12.859 --> 01:51:15.241
"Don't show your presents to Dad because it will depress him,"

01:51:15.301 --> 01:51:17.302
because he thinks it's a waste of money.

01:51:17.462 --> 01:51:20.925
"That didn't stop us from having fun,"

01:51:20.985 --> 01:51:21.505
But still.

01:51:23.006 --> 01:51:26.368
On December 24, 1977,

01:51:26.369 --> 01:51:27.949
Chaplin is particularly tired.

01:51:29.270 --> 01:51:29.971
But as usual,

01:51:30.091 --> 01:51:31.172
Ouna had big plans.

01:51:31.952 --> 01:51:33.453
The whole family is gathered in Vevey.

01:51:33.473 --> 01:51:37.556
"It was the big Christmas case."

01:51:37.557 --> 01:51:39.777
There was a large fir tree at the entrance,

01:51:40.718 --> 01:51:41.359
The gifts.

01:51:42.367 --> 01:51:42.867
everywhere,

01:51:43.908 --> 01:51:44.909
He really spoiled us.

01:51:46.310 --> 01:51:46.811
That evening,

01:51:48.432 --> 01:51:50.654
Chaplin cannot finish the evening with the whole family.

01:51:52.955 --> 01:51:56.178
He then asked to be escorted to his room.

01:52:01.843 --> 01:52:07.307
Ouna leaves her door ajar so he can hear the children's shouts when they open their presents.

01:52:09.659 --> 01:52:12.642
But in the early hours of December 25, 1977,

01:52:13.983 --> 01:52:16.665
He fell peacefully into his sleep.

01:52:32.077 --> 01:52:34.339
That's
where I saw my mother cry for the first time in my life.

01:52:34.920 --> 01:52:36.101
She never did it in front of us.

01:52:37.242 --> 01:52:38.643
That was a terrible shock for me.

01:52:39.235 --> 01:52:40.476
It happens if the timing is right.

01:52:40.477 --> 01:52:42.779
He left at Christmas.

01:52:54.639 --> 01:52:55.639
Until my last breath,

01:52:56.640 --> 01:52:59.141
Chaplin's life was therefore marked by irony.

01:53:01.202 --> 01:53:05.664
The one that allowed him to depict the world and its suffering with humor and tenderness.

01:53:06.484 --> 01:53:08.145
The one who helped him respond to the attacks.

01:53:09.545 --> 01:53:13.267
The one who gave life to Charlie Chaplin and made him immortal.

01:53:14.535 --> 01:53:14.876
Strangely,

01:53:14.876 --> 01:53:15.636
He will never be lacking.

01:53:15.676 --> 01:53:16.176
Chaplin,

01:53:16.456 --> 01:53:18.157
since he may no longer be here,

01:53:18.297 --> 01:53:19.357
but his work,

01:53:19.637 --> 01:53:20.418
his invention,

01:53:20.798 --> 01:53:22.298
It will always make people happy.

01:53:22.478 --> 01:53:23.079
sad,

01:53:23.219 --> 01:53:24.579
It will always affect people.

01:53:24.659 --> 01:53:25.220
So it's alive.

01:53:25.280 --> 01:53:26.220
somewhere.

01:53:26.380 --> 01:53:28.441
If anyone deserves the term genius,

01:53:28.781 --> 01:53:29.562
That's definitely Chaplin.

01:53:30.382 --> 01:53:31.222
Without a doubt.

01:53:41.399 --> 01:53:43.724
A quote from Stéphane Sfaye that I've always really liked,

01:53:43.804 --> 01:53:46.349
It is "Men need gods to exist,

01:53:46.389 --> 01:53:49.455
But the gods need certain men to prove they exist.

01:53:49.475 --> 01:53:51.139
I think Chappie is very much a part of it.

01:54:33.237 --> 01:54:38.159
Life can be wonderful if you

01:54:38.339 --> 01:54:40.020
Don't be afraid.

01:54:40.021 --> 01:54:41.541
Everything you need,

01:54:41.581 --> 01:54:43.081
That's courage.

01:54:43.542 --> 01:54:46.403
imagination and a little finger.

01:54:46.923 --> 01:54:48.664
The hydra has shown so many faces,

01:54:48.665 --> 01:54:49.684
The hilarious Charlie Chaplin,

01:54:49.824 --> 01:54:50.885
the sad Calvéro,

01:54:51.025 --> 01:54:51.985
the man who loved women,

01:54:52.045 --> 01:54:52.545
young,

01:54:52.726 --> 01:54:53.246
too young

01:54:53.626 --> 01:54:54.866
the vanquisher of the powerful,

01:54:54.867 --> 01:54:56.067
the extremely wealthy adventurer,

01:54:56.487 --> 01:54:59.408
Hollywood's enfant terrible and the solitary recluse of Vevey.

01:54:59.869 --> 01:55:04.070
Attempting to uncover the truth of genius always requires looking beyond.

01:55:04.851 --> 01:55:10.153
The evening dedicated to Charlie Chaplin and the 100th anniversary of Charlot continues on France 2 with a film,

01:55:10.593 --> 01:55:12.054
one of his greatest masterpieces.

01:55:12.474 --> 01:55:13.975
You have just discovered what goes on behind the scenes,

01:55:13.995 --> 01:55:14.495
here is...

01:55:14.575 --> 01:55:15.456
The Dictator,

01:55:15.596 --> 01:55:16.817
his most visionary film,

01:55:17.037 --> 01:55:21.021
written in 1936 and published in 1940,

01:55:21.061 --> 01:55:25.065
He perceived the dangers of Hitler's madness before anyone else.

01:55:25.446 --> 01:55:26.026
See you very soon.

